{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:37:40.361Z","ordinal":105119,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20bb2-48c0-7db0-bfc5-137d3a66f0eb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-6853f1f8-340f-488e-b229-3dd56cea1ac0","process_id":"51761","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...HEAD; rg -n 'context maturity|maturity assessment|context inventory|sourceVersion|context_budget|sourceTimeout|durable knowledge|memory promotion|context retrieval' cli/src docs/research/context-engineering"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git diff --stat origin/release/v1.3.0...HEAD; rg -n 'context maturity|maturity assessment|context inventory|sourceVersion|context_budget|sourceTimeout|durable knowledge|memory promotion|context retrieval' cli/src docs/research/context-engineering"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" cli/src/agent.ts                                   | 173 +++++-\n cli/src/audit_export.ts                            |   9 +-\n cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts   |   5 +-\n cli/src/core/context_inventory.ts                  | 673 +++++++++++++++++++++\n cli/src/core/objective.ts                          |   2 +-\n cli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts                     |  71 ++-\n cli/src/core/state.ts                              |   5 +\n cli/src/knowledge.ts                               | 157 +++--\n cli/src/repl.ts                                    |  10 +\n cli/src/session.ts                                 |  20 +-\n cli/src/session_export.ts                          |  37 +-\n cli/src/sidecar.ts                                 |   2 +\n cli/src/slash/catalog.ts                           |   1 +\n cli/src/slash/extension_commands.ts                |   5 +-\n cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts                | 288 +++++++++\n cli/test/audit_export.test.ts                      |   7 +-\n cli/test/context_inventory.test.ts                 | 634 +++++++++++++++++++\n cli/test/dv1_structured_attempts.test.ts           |  10 +\n cli/test/knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts         |  84 +++\n cli/test/persistence_protection.test.ts            |  14 +-\n cli/test/slash_router.test.ts                      |   4 +-\n cli/test/turn_verdict_evidence.test.ts             |   4 +-\n cli/test/workspace_trust.test.ts                   |  21 +-\n docs/USER_MANUAL.md                                |   6 +-\n .../context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | 202 +++++++\n docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md                        |   2 +-\n docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md                                |   7 +\n 27 files changed, 2313 insertions(+), 140 deletions(-)\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:1:# Nexus context maturity and inventory\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:20:The current `/context maturity` output is computed from one content-free on-demand inventory and can change with observed session evidence. On the deterministic command fixture used here, it reports navigability 2 — Exploratory, retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and compounding value 1 — Ad hoc (no durable memory was present in that fixture). Ratings remain independent and do not claim a managed maturity level.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:27:| Compounding value | 1 — Ad hoc in the no-memory fixture and when only a project-knowledge catalog entry is present; 2 — Exploratory only when a durable note or compaction link is observed in carried session context | Session state, compaction links, and bounded request manifests persist source references without copying context text. Operator-only promotion preserves provenance, unverified validation state, repository scope and retention; legacy entries migrate as unverified; expiry is enforced; model writes and automatic extraction are disabled. | Held-out evidence that persistent memory improves engineering outcomes is not measured; the existing durable knowledge store has repository scope only. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:35:Add a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that reuse `AutonomousAgent` getters, `DurableTaskState`/`SessionManager`, existing token estimates, `KnowledgeGraph`, and the common slash router. The inventory stores metadata and token estimates, not prompt plaintext or content hashes. Existing provider adapters remain the only inference transport boundary; this feature does not call providers.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:43:- `/context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]` measures current client-visible sources on demand and optionally stores a content-free session snapshot; `/context maturity [--json]` accepts the same budget/item limits and emits a deterministic four-dimension assessment with evidence, gaps, limitations, and next improvements. The default total source-collection budget is 2,000 ms. The same budget applies sequentially across the whole collection pass, so source order is deterministic and remaining sources are marked timed out after exhaustion.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:63:6. Context inspection and maturity assessment are available through the shared REPL/TUI slash router and JSON output is parseable.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:108:After rebasing onto PR #739, focused checks passed on the rebased source: context inventory 14/14, provider wire matrix 90/90, agent harness 90/90, slash router 39/39, knowledge controls 3/3, session durable fields 4/4, and persistence protection 27/27. The CLI build passed. On snapshot `48bb93f2` (based on `cebb31ac`, before PR #742), the full turn-semantics suite passed 37/37 and the focused long-step case passed 1/1 after the runtime binaries were placed where the CLI resolves them. After rebasing onto PR #742 at `a57c6c24`, exact-current-source checks passed on `b588d970`: CLI build, context inventory 14/14, knowledge controls 3/3, and provider wire matrix 90/90. At `03b62aaf`, `make build` passed, then `make test` was run with isolated CI-like workspace/runtime fixtures. Rust core passed 53/53, and scope fixtures/security gates passed; the aggregate command failed. Its aggregate test count was not available from the sharded runner output. The isolated `eval_dataset.test.ts` and standalone server-profile eval both fail closed before inference with `compiler exposure could not be checked; refusing qualification`; the gateway saw only the model-list probe, not a chat request. The version-probe test initially rejected the temporary `/tmp` runtime root; a retry used `/opt/nexus-eval-ci-runtime` and a private 128 MiB tmpfs with the required owner-only mount mode, but the host's bubblewrap could not access the workspace through its `/tmp` parent path. No protected fixture or guard was changed to bypass these checks. The D-04 behavior test exposed an obsolete assertion that expected model-originated `manage_knowledge` to persist durable memory. The test now asserts that this call is rejected and creates no knowledge file; `turn_verdict_evidence.test.ts` passes 26/26. After rebasing onto the latest `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `10942d41`, the focused checks before budget work passed: context inventory 14/14, knowledge controls 3/3, provider wire matrix 90/90, and turn verdict 26/26. The bounded-budget and prompt-provenance implementation passed `npm run build`, `context_inventory.test.ts` 16/16, knowledge controls 3/3, provider wire matrix 90/90, slash router 39/39, persistence protection 27/27, and skill injection 15/15 on exact snapshot `2502ae1b`. The corrected `make test` on snapshot `2502ae1b` passed core 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures and security gates, but failed overall in the CLI shard: 2,493 completed segments, 3 failures, and a timeout in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. Focused reruns show the dataset failure came from the local shared-checkout mode of the trusted evaluator helper, and the compaction file completes when the watchdog allows its declared 900-second test timeout. Two of the three CLI failures remain unclassified because the shard output was truncated. The full suite has not been rerun after correcting those local conditions or after rebasing onto `cd755b3e`; repository-wide qualification remains pending.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:116:- Operator-only memory promotion now carries metadata and expiry enforcement, but no held-out task-quality evaluation establishes that durable memories improve results. Existing schema-1 records are migrated additively when a writable load occurs; read-only loads label them in memory without rewriting their files.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:129:The context inventory previously labeled every skill catalog item `profile` scope, so repository candidate changes could not list workspace skills among the invalidated repository items. Workspace skill items now use `repository` scope, while global skills remain `profile`; both report freshness as `unknown` because the inventory does not re-read or persist a skill content digest. A regression assertion covers those scope labels and prior workspace-skill invalidation. `npm --prefix cli run typecheck` passed in a clean detached snapshot at `f7544181` using isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`; the targeted test is still unrun because the other worktree holds the shared `SUITE` claim. XERJ search found the existing skill content digest and qualification invalidation path (`cli/src/core/skill_activation.ts:67`, `cli/src/core/skills_qualification.ts:126`) and the catalog refresh/read implementation (`cli/src/skills.ts:219`, `cli/src/skills.ts:421`). We retain `unknown` rather than persist content digests in diagnostics, consistent with the context inventory's privacy boundary.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:172:On rebased source head `40c2194a`, context inventory items carry a content-free source version made from the normalized record update timestamp and validation state. A new capture compares those markers with the previous saved inventory and reports when the prior memory record changed; the current memory claim remains `unknown` because its underlying evidence is not revalidated. Source references remain in their existing bounded field, and the marker survives session save/resume and JSON/Markdown export. Unsafe version metadata is omitted or normalized before it reaches diagnostics. `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 17/17 and `npm run build` passed with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` on this exact head. The full `make test` result above predates this follow-up; it has not been rerun on `40c2194a`. The four maturity ratings do not change. No provider behavior changed.\ncli/src/session_export.ts:198:    for (const item of contextInventory.items) out.push(`- \\`${item.id}\\` ${item.sourceType} — ${item.sourceLocation}; scope=${item.scope}; observed=${item.observedAt}; freshness=${item.freshness}${item.freshnessRule ? ` (${item.freshnessRule})` : \"\"}${item.sourceVersion ? `; source-version=\\`${encodeURIComponent(item.sourceVersion)}\\`` : \"\"}; trust=${item.trust}; via=${item.retrievalMethod}${item.sourceRefs?.length ? `; refs=${item.sourceRefs.join(\",\")}` : \"\"}`);\ncli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:35:  sourceVersion: string;\ncli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:96:  const sourceDir = versionDir(value.sourceVersion);\ncli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:566:      if (!verifyInstalledRuntime(saved, sameVersion ? journal.sourceVersion : journal.targetVersion, options.timeoutMs).healthy && sameVersion) throw new Error(\"Preserved source package failed runtime validation; retained for manual intervention\");\ncli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:575:    const health = verifyInstalledRuntime(journal.sourceInstallDir, journal.sourceVersion, options.timeoutMs);\ncli/src/upgrade_journal.ts:585:    return { recovered:true, action:early ? \"cleaned_up\" : \"rolled_back\", details:`Restored verified source release ${journal.sourceVersion}.` };\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:939:    return outcome.recovered ? { success:true, revertedTo:recorded.sourceVersion } : { success:false, error:outcome.details };\ncli/src/upgrade.ts:1112:      sourceVersion:installed.version, sourceInstallDir:installed.installRoot || path.join(libNexus, installed.version),\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:198:    // Sensitive content is not eligible for durable memory promotion. Do not\ncli/src/knowledge.ts:300:   * @deprecated Conversation-derived memory promotion is disabled. Promote\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:294:  const usage = \"Usage: /context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>] | /context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]\";\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:485:    const sourceVersion = JSON.stringify([updatedAt, validationStatus]);\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:487:    const recordChanged = Boolean(previous?.sourceVersion !== undefined && previous.sourceVersion !== sourceVersion);\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:500:      sourceVersion,\ncli/src/core/spine_handlers.ts:68:          error: \"Model tool calls cannot promote durable knowledge. Use the explicit operator command /knowledge set or nexus knowledge set after reviewing the source.\",\ncli/src/core/scheduler.ts:497:      case \"lift_context_budget\":\ncli/src/core/operation_runner_execution.ts:313:      options: [{ label: \"lift this unit's context budget\", action: { kind: \"lift_context_budget\" } }],\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:27:  sourceVersion?: string;\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:214:  sourceVersion?: string;\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:285:        ...(item.sourceVersion && safeSourceVersion(item.sourceVersion) ? { sourceVersion: item.sourceVersion } : {}),\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:562:    Array.isArray(snapshot.items) && snapshot.items.length <= DEFAULT_MAX_ITEMS && snapshot.items.every((item) => item && safeText(item.id, 80) && safeText(item.sourceType, 80) && safeText(item.sourceLocation) && scopes.includes(item.scope) && safeText(item.observedAt, 80) && freshness.includes(item.freshness) && (item.freshnessRule === undefined || safeText(item.freshnessRule)) && (item.freshness === \"unknown\" || safeText(item.freshnessRule)) && (item.sourceVersion === undefined || safeSourceVersion(item.sourceVersion)) && trust.includes(item.trust) && safeText(item.retention) && safeText(item.inclusionReason) && safeText(item.retrievalMethod, 100) && Number.isFinite(item.estimatedTokens) && item.estimatedTokens >= 0 && (item.sourceRefs === undefined || (Array.isArray(item.sourceRefs) && item.sourceRefs.length <= 100 && item.sourceRefs.every((ref) => safeText(ref, 200))))) &&\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:669:    ...snapshot.items.map((item) => `${item.id} ${item.sourceType} @ ${item.sourceLocation} [${item.scope}; ${item.freshness}${item.freshnessRule ? ` (${item.freshnessRule})` : \"\"}${item.sourceVersion ? `; source-version=${encodeURIComponent(item.sourceVersion)}` : \"\"}; ${item.trust}] ${item.estimatedTokens} est. tokens; via ${item.retrievalMethod}`),\ncli/src/core/operation_schema.ts:38:  \"lift_context_budget\",\ncli/src/core/operation.ts:94:  | { kind: \"lift_context_budget\" }\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":891939713}},"started_at_ms":1795495059469,"completed_at_ms":1795495060361}}
