{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:20:25.433Z","ordinal":107529,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c23-8f96-7433-9b0c-25c42cdbc4cc","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bce3ca0a-4b43-412c-a59b-db3b573dd950","process_id":"67385","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | tail -n 70"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"nl -ba docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","name":"CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","path":"docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"   133\tAfter `release/v1.3.0` advanced to `7ed39059`, the implementation branch rebased cleanly. This release update adds workflow/cache CI changes and a workflow parity test; the source feature changes are unchanged. On detached exact-source snapshot `049a6077`, `npm --prefix cli run typecheck` and `make build` passed with isolated `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`; Rust release and CLI builds completed. At 2026-11-23 16:11 UTC, the AC-2 claim owner PID and all processes referencing its worktree were absent; its mock gateway had also exited. The claim was still less than 24 hours old, so it was not broken. The `SUITE` claim was taken after it disappeared. Another process began a sequence of isolated CLI tests before our test reservation; the new skill-scope regression and full `make test` are waiting until that process finishes, to keep tests serial. No test result is inferred from the build.\n   134\t\n   135\t## Validation update — 2026-11-23\n   136\t\n   137\tOn exact source head `976ba97d` (base `db9f6f98`, `release/v1.3.0`): `make build` passed using isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and the worktree-local Cargo target. Under Node 24.11.1, `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 16/16, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` passed 3/3, and `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` passed 90/90. These tests cover deterministic assessment and insufficient evidence, request/source provenance through save/resume/compaction/export, bounded and failed retrieval, freshness invalidation, scoped durable memory and model-write denial, and the provider adapter request matrix. They do not establish provider receipt of manifests or held-out memory value.\n   138\t\n   139\tThe dedicated `tui_maturity_e2e.test.ts` was run on that same head and failed after 190.4 seconds: the pseudo-terminal driver did not observe a terminal result for the scripted 35-step turn within its 180-second wait; the TUI had reached step 18. After the driver deadline, fixture cleanup removed the workspace while the sidecar was still unwinding, which caused follow-on persistence and workspace-state errors in the terminal event. Those cleanup errors are consequences of the timeout and are not evidence that persistence failed during an uninterrupted run. A diagnostic-only comparison on the release baseline (`db9f6f98`) reached 22 tool cycles within the same 180-second driver wait; request spacing averaged 8.38 seconds on baseline versus 9.85 seconds on the candidate run, and mock provider response times were below 2 seconds in both traces. This is a possible client-side throughput regression signal, not a controlled attribution: the runs were sequential on a loaded shared host, and no repeat or randomized paired run was completed. The temporary trace instrumentation was removed and no product code was changed from this comparison. The actual cause of the slower candidate step rate is not established. Host load and unrelated agent activity are contemporaneous confounders, not proof of causation. TUI end-to-end qualification therefore remains failed/unverified; the timeout must not be counted as a pass, and the possible throughput regression needs a controlled follow-up.\n   140\t\n   141\tThe full `make test` run described above was on pre-rebase snapshot `2502ae1b`, not `976ba97d`. It was manually interrupted after more than two hours while progressing through remaining CLI tests, after multiple CLI failures appeared; no final shard summary or overall exit result was collected. This is an incomplete historical run, not a pass. The corrected, completed full-suite result on snapshot `0b9feaae` is recorded in the latest validation update below. No inference-provider changes or provider-specific behavior were introduced.\n   142\t\n   143\tOn exact source head `dafe4fa2` (base `db9f6f98`, `release/v1.3.0`), durable project knowledge context explicitly carries `freshness: unknown` and a reason in `/context inspect`; prompt rendering labels each retained entry `freshness: unknown` because its source references are not revalidated. Request manifest construction now derives the aggregate estimate from the same per-message and tool counts it records; a deterministic assertion matches `calculateContextBudget`, including tool calls and capped references. `npm run build` passed; `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 17/17; the provider wire matrix passed 90/90 on this head. `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` passed 3/3 and `slash_router.test.ts` 39/39 after the preceding memory-freshness change. A synthetic microbenchmark measured 50.4% lower local manifest-build time on its stated fixture; it is not an end-to-end throughput result. No source digest or memory invalidation mechanism was added.\n   144\t\n   145\tA TUI E2E rerun during this work failed before any inference activity: after five seconds the PTY driver expected `thinking · 0:0` but the screen still showed `waiting for the agent`. Subsequent persistence notices occurred during driver/fixture teardown; a preserved fixture's existing committed message log validated after teardown, so those notices do not establish an uninterrupted-run persistence defect. This run does not measure the optimized manifest path's effect on TUI throughput. TUI qualification and the possible end-to-end throughput regression remain open.\n   146\t\n   147\tOn current source/documentation head `5a5eb68a`, `harness.test.ts` passed 90/90 in 80.7 seconds with isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`. It exercises the agent loop, context admission and compaction, worktree behavior, and simulated provider responses. This focused harness result does not replace the incomplete repository-wide test run or the failed PTY E2E check.\n   148\t\n   149\t### Validation update — 2026-11-23, TUI rerun\n   150\t\n   151\tOn the current candidate (`33e744c9`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `db9f6f98`), `tui_maturity_e2e.test.ts` passed 1/1 in 70.1 seconds, including the scripted multi-step turn, context inspection, resume, and export assertions. The same E2E test then passed 1/1 on the release baseline (`db9f6f98`) in 47.0 seconds. This was one sequential pair on the same host, not a randomized or repeated benchmark; the candidate took about 23 seconds longer in this sample. Treat this as a throughput regression signal requiring controlled repeated runs, not a causal attribution or a qualification failure. It supersedes the earlier statement above that the latest PTY run was still failed/unverified: functional TUI E2E now passes, while comparative performance and full-suite qualification remain open. Earlier timeout runs remain recorded as historical failures.\n   152\t\n   153\tThe temporary failure-only PTY diagnostic was reverted after the candidate and baseline reruns. No inference provider or provider-specific behavior was changed. At that point the full repository suite had not been rerun on the current release base; see the later full-suite update. Independent review remains outstanding.\n   154\t\n   155\t### Validation update — 2026-11-23, full suite and export correction\n   156\t\n   157\t`make test-ci` initially stopped before running tests because the shared `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` fixture already existed and was non-empty. It was left untouched. The same repository fixture script was then run against unique temporary mount/runtime paths, preserving its 128 MiB tmpfs and permissions. On snapshot `62350f89` (before the export correction below), `make build` passed; `cargo test` exited successfully; the CLI shard reported 2,930 tests (2,918 passed, 8 failed, 4 skipped) and timed out in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`; terminal-scope reported 3,140 tests (3,109 passed, 18 failed, 13 skipped); security gates passed. The overall `make test` exited 1. Several failures were host qualification/toolchain/resource checks; the audit-export determinism failure was attributable to this change and was reproduced in `audit_export.test.ts`.\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\tOn corrected snapshot `0b9feaae` (branch `codex/context-maturity-v130`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `db9f6f98`), `make build` passed and the full `make test` completed with exit 2 using unique CI fixture roots; the existing shared `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` was not modified. Core Rust tests passed 53/53; TUI unit tests passed 406/406; lifecycle security gates passed. The CLI shard reported 2,930 completed tests, 7 failures, and a timeout in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`. The terminal-scope shard reported 3,140 tests: 3,112 passed, 15 failed, and 13 skipped. Failures observed include host compiler-exposure checks refusing qualification, eval fixture/runtime assumptions, and convergence/attempt-classification assertions; two T3 end-to-end checks also failed earlier in the same run. These are preserved as failures and have not been individually reproduced or proven environmental. The export-specific regression files pass on this source (`audit_export.test.ts` 17/17 and `context_inventory.test.ts` 17/17), and the TypeScript build passes, but repository-wide qualification is not green. Independent review remains outstanding. No inference provider was modified.\n   161\t\n   162\t### Validation update — 2026-11-23, rebased v1.3.0 exact-head completion\n   163\t\n   164\tThis update supersedes earlier statements above that full-suite qualification on the current release branch was outstanding. The implementation branch was rebased without conflicts onto `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `f4333a359b142e7440a75932506a36d7dbabb924`. Exact feature head: `eda532061b8f78c67ddc3ffe4e3c3621312fd4eb`. `make build` passed on the source worktree; focused context, memory, provider-wire, routing and session/export tests passed 158/158 on this head.\n   165\t\n   166\tThe full `make test` was run to completion on a detached snapshot at that exact head, with isolated `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, worktree-local Cargo outputs, and unique CI fixture/mount paths. It exited 0. Rust core passed 53/53; TUI passed 406/406. CLI shard one passed 3,165/3,169 with 4 skipped; CLI shard two passed 2,956/2,969 with 13 skipped. Terminal scope fixtures passed, and all lifecycle security gates passed, including dependency audits, secret scanning, diff hygiene, and documentation scanning. The early `ℹ fail` lines in nested fixture outputs are expected assertions from tests that verify rejection/failure behavior; both aggregate CLI shard summaries report zero failures. The existing shared CI fixture paths and owner checkout were not modified. No live inference was used and no inference provider was modified.\n   167\t\n   168\tThe detached validation snapshot used a dependency tree copied with symlinks preserved and the evaluator helper's local materialized file mode restored to the committed 0644 mode; neither correction changed tracked source. The run establishes local full-suite qualification for that exact source snapshot, not hosted CI, release qualification, installed acceptance, provider receipt of request manifests, or independent review. Claude owns review and merge from this point; no PR, push, merge, or tag was created here.\n   169\t\n   170\t### Validation update — 2026-11-23, durable-memory version invalidation\n   171\t\n   172\tOn rebased source head `40c2194a`, context inventory items carry a content-free source version made from the normalized record update timestamp and validation state. A new capture compares those markers with the previous saved inventory and reports when the prior memory record changed; the current memory claim remains `unknown` because its underlying evidence is not revalidated. Source references remain in their existing bounded field, and the marker survives session save/resume and JSON/Markdown export. Unsafe version metadata is omitted or normalized before it reaches diagnostics. `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 17/17 and `npm run build` passed with isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` on this exact head. The full `make test` result above predates this follow-up; it has not been rerun on `40c2194a`. The four maturity ratings do not change. No provider behavior changed.\n   173\t\n   174\t### Validation update — 2026-11-23, latest release rebase and full-suite result\n   175\t\n   176\tThe feature branch was rebased onto `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `56e644cf5f0b6d3c85b82dc3bfec958535ae2493`. On the then-current pre-rebase-follow-up snapshot `cabe335e83b2b4b870856e6edd949ae7d52f1489`, `make build` passed and `make test` completed with exit 2. Core Rust tests passed 53/53; TUI tests passed 406/406; one CLI shard reported 2,959 tests (2,945 passed, 1 failed, 13 skipped), and the other reported 3,179 tests (3,175 passed, 4 skipped). The failing assertion was `test/cloud_providers.test.ts`: operator cancellation during a streaming response exceeded its 2-second bound and failed after the test runner's 300-second timeout. Scope fixtures and lifecycle/security gates passed. This is a recorded failure, not a green full-suite result.\n   177\t\n   178\tThe cancellation test was then run five times sequentially with isolated `HOME` and ephemeral mock-provider ports; all five passed in 137–147 ms. Source inspection confirms the caller signal is wired into `StreamWatchdog`, which aborts the fetch signal, and `readSse` cancels its reader on error. These repeats do not explain the full-shard timeout, so the intermittent failure remains unresolved and must not be classified as environmental or fixed. On the subsequently rebased current source, focused tests passed: `context_inventory.test.ts` 17/17, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` 3/3, `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` (all cases passed), session persistence/export/fork test files (all passed), and `audit_export.test.ts` 18/18. `make build` also passed with isolated `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and a worktree-local `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.\n   179\t\n   180\tThis rebase includes release-branch commits not present in the full-suite snapshot; full-suite status at the exact current head is therefore unverified. The four maturity ratings and their evidence remain unchanged. No inference provider was modified. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, a repeated comparative performance evaluation, and independent review remain outstanding; Claude owns PR review and merge. No push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n   181\t\n   182\t### Validation update — 2026-11-24, release tip refresh and focused requalification\n   183\t\n   184\tAfter the full-suite run, `origin/release/v1.3.0` advanced to `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3` with inference-submission budgeting and protocol-schema updates. The context branch was rebased onto that tip; source-tested head is `8d4bb77a1bdb076012e510244f054bc9d4f943f4`. On that head, `make build` passed. Sequential isolated tests passed: `context_inventory.test.ts` 17/17, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` 3/3, `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` 90/90, `audit_export.test.ts` 18/18, and `session_durable_fields.test.ts` 4/4. The initial inventory attempt failed because this worktree's custom in-repository Cargo target contained an oversized generated `libgit2.a`, which the candidate fingerprint correctly rejected; after removing that task-generated directory and rerunning with the normal ignored build outputs, inventory passed 17/17. The evidence-only documentation commit followed that tested source head. The pre-rebase full-suite failure remains the latest full-run evidence and is not represented as qualification of `8d4bb77a`.\n   185\t\n   186\tThe exact-head full run on predecessor `361a744f` completed `make test` with exit 2: core Rust 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures passed, and security lifecycle gates passed. CLI shard one completed 2,970 tests (2,949 passed, 8 failed, 13 skipped) before the 300-second per-file runner killed `compaction_continuity.test.ts`; shard two completed 2,699 tests (2,693 passed, 2 failed, 4 skipped) before the same runner killed `verify_hostile.test.ts`. Running `compaction_continuity.test.ts` directly on that exact snapshot passed 34/34 in 532.959 seconds, confirming that its declared workload exceeds the runner's 300-second default. The two T3 evaluator failures and several evaluator harness failures refused qualification because compiler exposure could not be checked; another evaluator test failed to find the selected stimulus, and a TUI cancellation timing assertion failed. Those failures remain recorded and unclassified; the second timeout has not been independently reproduced. The full suite must be rerun on current head, and the test-runner timeout mismatch and evaluator failures remain qualification issues. The four maturity ratings do not change. No provider was modified; no push, PR, merge, or tag was created.\n   187\t\n   188\t### Validation update — 2026-11-24, corrected full suite at release snapshot\n   189\t\n   190\tThe exact feature snapshot `2b623b4473271111614a80a551b47bfce4297c47` is based on the requested `release/v1.3.0` line. Before this validation, the first full-suite attempt failed evaluator fixtures because the physical checkout had materialized `eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs` as group-writable, which the evaluator correctly rejects; two long CLI files also exceeded the default 300-second per-file timeout. The Git-recorded mode was `100644`. For the corrected run, only the snapshot's local materialized mode was restored to `0644` and the timeout was raised to 900 seconds; no tracked source was changed. The evaluator and long-file cases were rerun, then the complete `make test` was executed serially under the SUITE claim with isolated HOME, worktree-local Cargo output, and unique temporary fixture roots.\n   191\t\n   192\tResults from the corrected run: Rust core tests passed 53/53, Rust TUI tests passed 406/406, and the remaining Rust integration groups passed 9/9. The CLI suite reported 3,053 tests: 3,052 passed, 0 failed, and 1 skipped. Terminal acceptance reported 3,111 tests: 3,095 passed, 0 failed, and 16 skipped. The terminal scope fixtures passed. Every lifecycle security gate reported success, including Node and Rust dependency audits, credential scanning, diff hygiene, and forbidden-documentation scanning. The run output contained no Makefile `[!] FAILED` step marker or final `make test: one or more steps failed` message.\n   193\t\n   194\tThe outer validation command nevertheless returned exit code 1 after the security gates printed success, with `zsh:42: PIPESTATUS[0]: parameter not set`. Thus the component summaries are green, but the aggregate shell-wrapper status was not captured cleanly; this record does not label the aggregate command as a verified exit-0 run. The exact command output is retained at `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-2b623b44-fixed.log`. The command's own evaluator tmpfs and runtime roots were removed after its process exited; the separate isolated HOME is retained for diagnostics. The owner checkout and the shared fixture paths were not modified.\n   195\t\n   196\tThese results supersede the older predecessor-only suite reports as the most recent full-suite evidence, but establish local component qualification only. The maturity ratings remain Navigability 2 — Exploratory, Retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, Freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and Compounding value 1 in the no-memory fixture / 2 only when durable context is observed. There is still no held-out evidence that durable memory improves task outcomes, no measured retrieval SLO or end-to-end latency distribution, and durable-memory freshness remains unknown where source fingerprints are unavailable. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a fresh full run whose outer command exits zero remain outstanding. No inference provider was modified, and no push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n   197\t\n   198\t### Validation update — 2026-11-24, current rebased release snapshot\n   199\t\n   200\tOn implementation head `52b54573264a1ac563119a9f318e57affc3a2753`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `d03e6199f37bd024f17a807f00ed261291f8a02c`, `make build` passed in an isolated snapshot. The subsequent exact-head `make test` completed its Rust and terminal-security stages but failed in the second CLI shard. Rust core passed 53/53, Rust TUI passed 406/406, and the other Rust integration groups passed (1/1, 3/3, 4/4, and 1/1); the first CLI shard reported 3,108/3,112 passed with 4 skipped. The second CLI shard reported 3,057 tests: 3,043 passed, 1 failed, and 13 skipped. Its sole failure was `test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, “the same trajectory with a passing verifier is VERIFIED only through the verifier run”: expected `execution === COMPLETED`, received `FAILED`. Terminal scope fixtures passed and all lifecycle security gates printed success, but `make test` ended with `make: *** [Makefile:67: test] Error 1`; this is a failed aggregate run.\n   201\t\n   202\tThe complete `turn_semantics.test.ts` file was then run alone on the same snapshot with an isolated HOME and passed 37/37 in 94.2 seconds. This non-reproduction does not erase the full-suite failure or establish its cause. The exact full-run log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-52b54573-built.log`. No source was changed during these runs. The release branch has since advanced beyond this tested base; the implementation must be rebased and requalified at its current tip before making a release-level claim. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a clean exact-current full-suite run remain outstanding. No live inference was used and no inference provider, PR, release tag, or remote branch was changed.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":715781554}},"started_at_ms":1795501224717,"completed_at_ms":1795501225433}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:20:25.567Z","ordinal":107530,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20c36-765f-7701-babf-dc83917e9a17","call_id":"call_139edd784e7c4c23987f54215195c8c0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 5374)\nTotal output lines: 70\n\n   133\tAfter `release/v1.3.0` advanced to `7ed39059`, the implementation branch rebased cleanly. This release update adds workflow/cache CI changes and a workflow parity test; the source feature changes are unchanged. On detached exact-source snapshot `049a6077`, `npm --prefix cli run typecheck` and `make build` passed with isolated `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`; Rust release and CLI builds completed. At 2026-11-23 16:11 UTC, the AC-2 claim owner PID and all processes referencing its worktree were absent; its mock gateway had also exited. The claim was still less than 24 hours old, so it was not broken. The `SUITE` claim was taken after it disappeared. Another process began a sequence of isolated CLI tests before our test reservation; the new skill-scope regression and full `make test` are waiting until that process finishes, to keep tests serial. No test result is inferred from the build.\n   134\t\n   135\t## Validation update — 2026-11-23\n   136\t\n   137\tOn exact source head `976ba97d` (base `db9f6f98`, `release/v1.3.0`): `make build` passed using isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` and the worktree-local Cargo target. Under Node 24.11.1, `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 16/16, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` passed 3/3, and `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` passed 90/90. These tests cover deterministic assessment and insufficient evidence, request/source provenance through save/resume/compaction/export, bounded and failed retrieval, freshness invalidation, scoped durable memory and model-write denial, and the provider adapter request matrix. They do not establish provider receipt of manifests or held-out memory value.\n   138\t\n   139\tThe dedicated `tui_maturity_e2e.test.ts` was run on that same head and failed after 190.4 seconds: the pseudo-terminal driver did not observe a terminal result for the scripted 35-step turn within its 180-second wait; the TUI had reached step 18. After the driver deadline, fixture cleanup removed the workspace while the sidecar was still unwinding, which caused follow-on persistence and workspace-state errors in the terminal event. Those cleanup errors are consequences of the timeout and are not evidence that persistence failed during an uninterrupted run. A diagnostic-only comparison on the release baseline (`db9f6f98`) reached 22 tool cycles within the same 180-second driver wait; request spacing averaged 8.38 seconds on baseline versus 9.85 seconds on the candidate run, and mock provider response times were below 2 seconds in both traces. This is a possible client-side throughput regression signal, not a controlled attribution: the runs were sequential on a loaded shared host, and no repeat or randomized paired run was completed. The temporary trace instrumentation was removed and no product code was changed from this comparison. The actual cause of the slower candidate step rate is not established. Host load and unrelated agent activity are contemporaneous confounders, not proof of causation. TUI end-to-end qualification therefore remains failed/unverified; the timeout must not be counted as a pass, and the possible throughput regression needs a controlled follow-up.\n   140\t\n   141\tThe full `make test` run described above was on pre-rebase snapshot `2502ae1b`, not `976ba97d`. It was manually interrupted after more than two hours while progressing through remaining CLI tests, after multiple CLI failures appeared; no final shard summary or overall exit result was collected. This is an incomplete historical run, not a pass. The corrected, completed full-suite result on snapshot `0b9feaae` is recorded in the latest validation update below. No inference-provider changes or provider-specific behavior were introduced.\n   142\t\n   143\tOn exact source head `dafe4fa2` (base `db9f6f98`, `release/v1.3.0`), durable project knowledge context explicitly carries `freshness: unknown` and a reason in `/context inspect`; prompt rendering labels each retained entry `freshness: unknown` because its source references are not revalidated. Request manifest construction now derives the aggregate estimate from the same per-message and tool counts it records; a deterministic assertion matches `calculateContextBudget`, including tool calls and capped references. `npm run build` passed; `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 17/17; the provider wire matrix passed 90/90 on this head. `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` passed 3/3 and `slash_router.test.ts` 39/39 after the preceding memory-freshness change. A synthetic microbenchmark measured 50.4% lower local manifest-build time on its stated fixture; it is not an end-to-end throughput result. No source digest or memory invalidation mechanism was added.\n   144\t\n   145\tA TUI E2E rerun during this work failed before any inference activity: after five seconds the PTY driver expected `thinking · 0:0` but the screen still showed `waiting for the agent`. Subsequent persistence notices occurred during driver/fixture teardown; a preserved fixture's existing committed message log validated after teardown, so those notices do not establish an uninterrupted-run persistence defect. This run does not measure the optimized manifest path's effect on TUI throughput. TUI qualification and the possible end-to-end throughput regression remain open.\n   146\t\n   147\tOn current source/documentation head `5a5eb68a`, `harness.test.ts` passed 90/90 in 80.7 seconds with isolated `HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME`. It exercises the agent loop, context admission and compaction, worktree behavior, and simulated provider responses. This focused harness result does not replace the incomplete repository-wide test run or the failed PTY E2E check.\n   148\t\n   149\t### Validation update — 2026-11-23, TUI rerun\n   150\t\n   151\tOn the current candidate (`33e744c9`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `db9f6f98`), `tui_maturity_e2e.test.ts` passed 1/1 in 70.1 seconds, including the scripted multi-step turn, context inspection, resume, and export assertions. The same E2E test then passed 1/1 on the release baseline (`db9f6f98`) in 47.0 seconds. This was one sequential pair on the same host, not a randomized or repeated benchmark; the candidate took about 23 seconds longer in this sample. Treat this as a throughput regression signal requiring controlled repeated runs, not a causal attribution or a qualification failure. It supersedes the earlier statement above that the latest PTY run was still failed/unverified: functional TUI E2E now passes, while comparative performance and full-suite qualification remain open. Earlier timeout runs remain recorded as historical failures.\n   152\t\n   153\tThe temporary failure-only PTY diagnostic was reverted after the candidate and baseline reruns. No inference provider or provider-specific behavior was changed. At that point the full repository suite had not been rerun on the current release base; see the later full-suite update. Independent review remains outstanding.\n   154\t\n   155\t### Validation update — 2026-11-23, full suite and export correction\n   156\t\n   157\t`make test-ci` initially stopped before running tests because the shared `/mnt/nexus-eval-ci` fixture already existed and was non-empty. It was left untouched. The same repository fixture script was then run against unique temporary mount/runtime paths, preserving its 128 MiB tmpfs and permissions. On snapshot `62350f89` (before the export correction below), `make build` passed; `cargo test` exited successfully; the CLI shard reported 2,930 tests (2,918 passed, 8 failed, 4 skipped) and timed out in `compaction_continuity.test.ts`; terminal-scop…1574 tokens truncated…ct current head is therefore unverified. The four maturity ratings and their evidence remain unchanged. No inference provider was modified. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, a repeated comparative performance evaluation, and independent review remain outstanding; Claude owns PR review and merge. No push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n   181\t\n   182\t### Validation update — 2026-11-24, release tip refresh and focused requalification\n   183\t\n   184\tAfter the full-suite run, `origin/release/v1.3.0` advanced to `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3` with inference-submission budgeting and protocol-schema updates. The context branch was rebased onto that tip; source-tested head is `8d4bb77a1bdb076012e510244f054bc9d4f943f4`. On that head, `make build` passed. Sequential isolated tests passed: `context_inventory.test.ts` 17/17, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` 3/3, `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` 90/90, `audit_export.test.ts` 18/18, and `session_durable_fields.test.ts` 4/4. The initial inventory attempt failed because this worktree's custom in-repository Cargo target contained an oversized generated `libgit2.a`, which the candidate fingerprint correctly rejected; after removing that task-generated directory and rerunning with the normal ignored build outputs, inventory passed 17/17. The evidence-only documentation commit followed that tested source head. The pre-rebase full-suite failure remains the latest full-run evidence and is not represented as qualification of `8d4bb77a`.\n   185\t\n   186\tThe exact-head full run on predecessor `361a744f` completed `make test` with exit 2: core Rust 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures passed, and security lifecycle gates passed. CLI shard one completed 2,970 tests (2,949 passed, 8 failed, 13 skipped) before the 300-second per-file runner killed `compaction_continuity.test.ts`; shard two completed 2,699 tests (2,693 passed, 2 failed, 4 skipped) before the same runner killed `verify_hostile.test.ts`. Running `compaction_continuity.test.ts` directly on that exact snapshot passed 34/34 in 532.959 seconds, confirming that its declared workload exceeds the runner's 300-second default. The two T3 evaluator failures and several evaluator harness failures refused qualification because compiler exposure could not be checked; another evaluator test failed to find the selected stimulus, and a TUI cancellation timing assertion failed. Those failures remain recorded and unclassified; the second timeout has not been independently reproduced. The full suite must be rerun on current head, and the test-runner timeout mismatch and evaluator failures remain qualification issues. The four maturity ratings do not change. No provider was modified; no push, PR, merge, or tag was created.\n   187\t\n   188\t### Validation update — 2026-11-24, corrected full suite at release snapshot\n   189\t\n   190\tThe exact feature snapshot `2b623b4473271111614a80a551b47bfce4297c47` is based on the requested `release/v1.3.0` line. Before this validation, the first full-suite attempt failed evaluator fixtures because the physical checkout had materialized `eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs` as group-writable, which the evaluator correctly rejects; two long CLI files also exceeded the default 300-second per-file timeout. The Git-recorded mode was `100644`. For the corrected run, only the snapshot's local materialized mode was restored to `0644` and the timeout was raised to 900 seconds; no tracked source was changed. The evaluator and long-file cases were rerun, then the complete `make test` was executed serially under the SUITE claim with isolated HOME, worktree-local Cargo output, and unique temporary fixture roots.\n   191\t\n   192\tResults from the corrected run: Rust core tests passed 53/53, Rust TUI tests passed 406/406, and the remaining Rust integration groups passed 9/9. The CLI suite reported 3,053 tests: 3,052 passed, 0 failed, and 1 skipped. Terminal acceptance reported 3,111 tests: 3,095 passed, 0 failed, and 16 skipped. The terminal scope fixtures passed. Every lifecycle security gate reported success, including Node and Rust dependency audits, credential scanning, diff hygiene, and forbidden-documentation scanning. The run output contained no Makefile `[!] FAILED` step marker or final `make test: one or more steps failed` message.\n   193\t\n   194\tThe outer validation command nevertheless returned exit code 1 after the security gates printed success, with `zsh:42: PIPESTATUS[0]: parameter not set`. Thus the component summaries are green, but the aggregate shell-wrapper status was not captured cleanly; this record does not label the aggregate command as a verified exit-0 run. The exact command output is retained at `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-2b623b44-fixed.log`. The command's own evaluator tmpfs and runtime roots were removed after its process exited; the separate isolated HOME is retained for diagnostics. The owner checkout and the shared fixture paths were not modified.\n   195\t\n   196\tThese results supersede the older predecessor-only suite reports as the most recent full-suite evidence, but establish local component qualification only. The maturity ratings remain Navigability 2 — Exploratory, Retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, Freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and Compounding value 1 in the no-memory fixture / 2 only when durable context is observed. There is still no held-out evidence that durable memory improves task outcomes, no measured retrieval SLO or end-to-end latency distribution, and durable-memory freshness remains unknown where source fingerprints are unavailable. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a fresh full run whose outer command exits zero remain outstanding. No inference provider was modified, and no push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n   197\t\n   198\t### Validation update — 2026-11-24, current rebased release snapshot\n   199\t\n   200\tOn implementation head `52b54573264a1ac563119a9f318e57affc3a2753`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `d03e6199f37bd024f17a807f00ed261291f8a02c`, `make build` passed in an isolated snapshot. The subsequent exact-head `make test` completed its Rust and terminal-security stages but failed in the second CLI shard. Rust core passed 53/53, Rust TUI passed 406/406, and the other Rust integration groups passed (1/1, 3/3, 4/4, and 1/1); the first CLI shard reported 3,108/3,112 passed with 4 skipped. The second CLI shard reported 3,057 tests: 3,043 passed, 1 failed, and 13 skipped. Its sole failure was `test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, “the same trajectory with a passing verifier is VERIFIED only through the verifier run”: expected `execution === COMPLETED`, received `FAILED`. Terminal scope fixtures passed and all lifecycle security gates printed success, but `make test` ended with `make: *** [Makefile:67: test] Error 1`; this is a failed aggregate run.\n   201\t\n   202\tThe complete `turn_semantics.test.ts` file was then run alone on the same snapshot with an isolated HOME and passed 37/37 in 94.2 seconds. This non-reproduction does not erase the full-suite failure or establish its cause. The exact full-run log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-52b54573-built.log`. No source was changed during these runs. The release branch has since advanced beyond this tested base; the implementation must be rebased and requalified at its current tip before making a release-level claim. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a clean exact-current full-suite run remain outstanding. No live inference was used and no inference provider, PR, release tag, or remote branch was changed.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c23-8f96-7433-9b0c-25c42cdbc4cc","create_time":1795501225.567664}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":48352,"sampled_through_sequence":48349,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
