{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:34:57.523Z","ordinal":107879,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c42-e8d0-7ec1-8d46-757074eef47b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-93208471-b25a-4c0e-8a2b-5ba1b37f5ba1","process_id":"11336","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 771 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json state,author,assignees,reviewRequests,reviews,comments,updatedAt --jq '{state,author:.author.login,assignees:[.assignees[].login],reviewRequests:[.reviewRequests[].login],updatedAt,reviews:[.reviews[] | {author:.author.login,state,submittedAt,body}],comments:[.comments[-5:][] | {author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 771 --repo mikeholownych/nexus-code --json state,author,assignees,reviewRequests,reviews,comments,updatedAt --jq '{state,author:.author.login,assignees:[.assignees[].login],reviewRequests:[.reviewRequests[].login],updatedAt,reviews:[.reviews[] | {author:.author.login,state,submittedAt,body}],comments:[.comments[-5:][] | {author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"assignees\":[],\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"coderabbitai\",\"body\":\"\\u003c!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003e [!IMPORTANT]\\n\\u003e ## Review skipped\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Auto reviews are disabled on base/target branches other than the default branch.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Please check the settings in the CodeRabbit UI or the `.coderabbit.yaml` file in this repository. To trigger a single review, invoke the `@coderabbitai review` command.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003e\\u003cpicture\\u003e\\u003csource media=\\\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\\\" srcset=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\\\"\\u003e\\u003cimg src=\\\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\\\" width=\\\"16\\\" height=\\\"16\\\" align=\\\"absmiddle\\\" alt=\\\"\\\"\\u003e\\u003c/picture\\u003e Run configuration\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003cbr\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e - **Source mode**: Auto\\n\\u003e - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n\\u003e - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n\\u003e - **Layers**: defaults\\n\\u003e - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n\\u003e - **Plan**: Advanced\\n\\u003e - **Run ID**: `17bbeb49-0b32-4ee0-9185-441bfa676ac4`\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e \\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e You can disable this status message by setting the `reviews.review_status` to `false` in the CodeRabbit configuration file.\\n\\u003e \\n\\u003e Use the checkbox below for a quick retry:\\n\\u003e - [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\\\"} --\\u003e Trigger review\\n\\n\\u003c!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:start --\\u003e\\n- [ ] \\u003c!-- {\\\"checkboxId\\\":\\\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\\\"} --\\u003e \\u003cstrong title=\\\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\\"\\u003eAutofix\\u003c/strong\\u003e · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n\\u003c!-- autopilot:end --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- tips_start --\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss\\u0026utm_medium=github\\u0026utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code\\u0026utm_content=771)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003e\\u003cstrong\\u003eShare\\u003c/strong\\u003e\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\u003cdl\\u003e\\n\\u003cdd\\u003e\\n\\u003cbr\\u003e\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A\\u0026url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai\\u0026mini=true\\u0026title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit\\u0026summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n\\u003c/dd\\u003e\\n\\u003c/dl\\u003e\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- tips_end --\\u003e\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-24T05:42:32Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Independent review at `7e58def9d65db39a24d5fe24bf9d32a0c85f50fc` — REQUEST CHANGES. The head has moved to `c615f6a1`, which changes four lines in two test files (the expectations of item 1) and no source, so item 2 applies to it unchanged.**\\n\\n**Blocking**\\n\\n1. **Two test files failed at `7e58def9` and pass on the base**: `audit_export` (17 pass, 2 fail: the warning text at line 142, and 11 files expected where there are now 12 at line 525) and `audit_command` (6 pass, 2 fail: `files: 11`, and the `--json` schema test). `c615f6a1` updates those expectations; CI on that head will show whether it is complete.\\n\\n2. **`nexus audit export` now runs git in a directory taken from recorded state without neutralising filters, and a clean filter there executes** (confirmed by running). `verifyCheckout` returns trusted for a plain repository with a `.git` directory. With `* filter=x` in `.gitattributes` and a `filter.x.clean` command in that repository's `.git/config`, calling `computeCandidateIdentitySync` with this PR's bounds ran the command twice (it wrote the marker file). `candidate.ts` runs `git status` with only `core.fsmonitor=false` and `core.hooksPath=/dev/null`, which does not stop clean filters; `git rev-parse` and `git config --get` run without those flags.\\n   The routine is shared, so the exposure exists wherever a candidate identity is computed. What is new is the caller: `audit_export.ts:646-647` puts it in front of whoever runs `audit export`, on whatever workspace the state names. An audit export should be safe to run on a workspace one does not trust; `nexus verify` already takes care here (a clean filter did not run in the review of #756).\\n   Fix: run git for this with configuration overrides that disable filters and fail closed, as the verify path does; or refuse a workspace whose `.git/config` or attributes set a filter; or, if neither, state the exposure in `docs/AUDIT.md` and report `unavailable`.\\n\\n**Not blocking**\\n\\n3. Receipts are computed on the active worktree path (`spine_handlers.ts:452`); the export uses the recorded workspace path. If the two differ, every receipt reports `mismatch`. Confirm they are the same directory, or say which is used.\\n4. An export with no receipts now always carries a `no_receipts` warning. Other empty cases are quiet, and this changes the warnings of every such bundle.\\n5. A mismatch is a warning and the export exits 0. That is a reasonable policy; it is not stated in the PR or in `docs/AUDIT.md`.\\n6. `docs/AUDIT.md` is not updated: the file list (line 70) and \\\"the two `receipts/` files\\\" (line 115) are now wrong.\\n7. The 50,000-entry and 256 MiB bounds have no test (raising all three bounds is caught only by the 10,001-receipt case), and removing the untrusted-checkout refusal fails nothing: there is no test with an untrusted checkout.\\n\\n**Held up**\\n\\n- The digest uses the same routine and defaults as the receipt; the lower limits make it throw, not produce a different digest. A bound that is hit reports `unavailable` (`candidate_scan_limit_exceeded`), never `matched`; receipt truncation reports `partial`.\\n- The new file goes through `generated()`: redaction, the sensitive-content check and a manifest hash like every other file. It holds ids and statuses only, no absolute paths; `checked_at` is the bundle's creation time.\\n- Reporting a mismatch as a match fails the binding test.\\n\\n**Tests at `7e58def9`:** `audit_bundle` 25/0, `audit_schema` 7/0, `leak_guard` 6/0, `verify_hostile` 46/0, `check_requirements` 28/0, `tsc` clean, `check_invariants` passes.\\n\\n**Not checked:** a byte-flip of the new file followed by `audit verify` (by reading it is covered by the manifest), an older `audit verify` on a new bundle, symlink and submodule digests, the complexity gate.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-24T05:59:06Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Re-review at `64a3b05302bc465882c092f279702290877c2a14` — REQUEST CHANGES. The head is now `3455d3f4`, which changes two lines of `audit_command.test.ts` and nothing else; everything about the source below applies to it.**\\n\\n**The blocker is not addressed.** Every commit since `7e58def9` touches test expectations only. `cli/src/core/candidate.ts` and `cli/src/audit_export.ts` are unchanged, and so is `docs/AUDIT.md`. Please do not merge this on green checks: the checks do not exercise a hostile workspace.\\n\\n**Programs configured in the workspace still run during `audit export`.** Each case below was run against both `computeCandidateIdentitySync` and the in-process `exportAuditBundle` with a seeded subject, on a throwaway repository whose tracked file had its mtime bumped so git had to re-hash it. \\\"Executed\\\" means the configured command wrote its marker file.\\n\\n| Vector | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| `filter.\\u003cx\\u003e.clean` via `.gitattributes` | executed |\\n| `filter.\\u003cx\\u003e.process` | executed (the export then reported `unavailable`) |\\n| `core.fsmonitor=\\u003ccommand\\u003e` | executed |\\n| `include.path` to a file that sets a filter | executed |\\n| `includeIf` to a file that sets a filter | executed |\\n| `core.attributesFile` naming the filter | executed |\\n| `.git/info/attributes` naming the filter | executed |\\n| `.git` as a file pointing at a gitdir elsewhere with `core.worktree` back at the workspace | executed (and `verifyCheckout` passes it) |\\n| `core.worktree` set, with a filter | executed |\\n| `filter.smudge`, `diff.textconv`, `core.sshCommand`, `core.pager`, `core.editor` | not executed |\\n| `post-index-change`, `reference-transaction`, `pre-auto-gc` hooks | not executed |\\n| an alias for `status`, a `.gitconfig` in the workspace, a bare repository in a subdirectory | not executed |\\n\\n`core.fsmonitor` runs although `git status` is given `-c core.fsmonitor=false`: another git call in the routine (`ls-files`, `rev-parse` or `config`) does not carry the override.\\n\\n**What a fix needs:** the same overrides on every git call the routine makes; filters and the fsmonitor disabled in a way that fails closed (command-line `-c` overrides, plus `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null`, `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, `GIT_ATTR_NOSYSTEM=1`), or a refusal with `unavailable` for any workspace whose configuration, includes or attributes name a filter or an fsmonitor; and a test with at least the clean-filter case that fails when the hardening is removed. There is no hostile-repository test today.\\n\\nOne thing to settle while fixing: the routine is shared with `agent.ts`, `spine_handlers.ts`, `worktree.ts`, `state.ts` and `operation_runner_execution.ts`. Changing how it hashes would change receipt digests; changing only what it allows to execute would not. With today's code a legitimate repository behaves correctly (plain, `* text=auto` with a CRLF file, and a real filter each report `matched`, then `mismatch` after an edit), but the real filter runs during the export.\\n\\n**Tests at `64a3b053`:** `audit_command` 7 pass, 1 fail (the expectation added by \\\"expect missing receipt binding warning\\\" asserts `no_receipts`, while the fixture has a receipt and reports `partial`); `3455d3f4` appears to correct that. `audit_export` 19/0, `audit_bundle` 25/0, `audit_schema` 7/0, `leak_guard` 6/0, `verify_hostile` 46/0, `verify_command` 18/0, `tsc` clean, `check_invariants` passes.\\n\\n**Still open from the first review:** items 3 to 7 (worktree path versus recorded workspace path; the `no_receipts` warning on every receipt-less export, which a test now asserts; the exit-status policy; `docs/AUDIT.md`; no test for the two scan bounds or an untrusted checkout).\\n\\n**Not checked:** the CLI entry end to end (it calls the same function), a registered submodule with a filter, the head `3455d3f4` beyond its diff.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-24T06:18:07Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"The blocker has a fix ready as a PR into this branch: #772 (\\\"do not hash a repository whose own Git configuration names a program\\\"). It adds a check in `audit_export.ts` before the candidate identity is computed and a test with five planted configurations; it does not touch `candidate.ts`, so receipt digests are unchanged. Merge it here, or reimplement it differently, and I will re-review. The newest commit here (`403f197d`) still changes test expectations only.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-24T06:28:38Z\"}],\"reviewRequests\":[],\"reviews\":[],\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-11-24T06:28:38Z\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":276833408}},"started_at_ms":1795502096245,"completed_at_ms":1795502097523}}
