{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:35:32.575Z","ordinal":107894,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c42-e8d0-7ec1-8d46-757074eef47b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-bf48b158-f344-4629-a898-52a28661542c","process_id":"92318","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md; rg -n 'computeCandidateIdentitySync|verifyCheckout|candidate.*fingerprint|freshness' cli/src/core/context_inventory.ts cli/src/audit_export.ts cli/src/core/candidate.ts cli/src/core/checkout_trust.ts; git status --short --branch; git rev-parse HEAD"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md; rg -n 'computeCandidateIdentitySync|verifyCheckout|candidate.*fingerprint|freshness' cli/src/core/context_inventory.ts cli/src/audit_export.ts cli/src/core/candidate.ts cli/src/core/checkout_trust.ts; git status --short --branch; git rev-parse HEAD"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \"<words>\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \"<words>\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \"<symbol>\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\" --verdict \"<what worked and what did not>\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:24:  freshness: ContextFreshness;\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:25:  freshnessRule?: string;\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:212:  freshness?: ContextFreshness;\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:213:  freshnessRule?: string;\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:276:      const freshness = item.freshnessRule ? item.freshness ?? \"unknown\" : \"unknown\";\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:283:        freshness,\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:284:        ...(item.freshnessRule ? { freshnessRule: metadataText(item.freshnessRule) } : {}),\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:315:    gaps.push(\"the previous context capture has no workspace fingerprint; repository freshness remains unknown\");\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:317:    gaps.push(\"current workspace state could not be fingerprinted; repository freshness remains unknown\");\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:374:/** Rebuild only what legacy/session records can establish; repository freshness remains unknown. */\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:434:      freshness: \"unknown\",\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:435:      freshnessRule: archived ? \"archived transcript is historical; no workspace fingerprint is retained\" : \"conversation history is historical and may describe an earlier workspace state\",\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:516:        : coverageGaps.length > 0 || items.some((item) => item.freshness === \"unknown\") || primary.metrics.omittedItems > 0 || supplemental.metrics.omittedItems > 0\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:527:  const invalidated = snapshot.items.some((item) => item.freshness === \"current\");\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:529:  const coverageGaps = [...new Set([...snapshot.coverageGaps, \"persisted context freshness was not revalidated against current session and workspace state\"])];\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:534:    items: snapshot.items.map((item) => item.freshness === \"current\"\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:535:      ? { ...item, freshness: \"unknown\", freshnessRule: \"persisted observation requires revalidation before it can be considered current\" }\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:551:  const freshness = [\"current\", \"stale\", \"unknown\"];\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:562:    Array.isArray(snapshot.items) && snapshot.items.length <= DEFAULT_MAX_ITEMS && snapshot.items.every((item) => item && safeText(item.id, 80) && safeText(item.sourceType, 80) && safeText(item.sourceLocation) && scopes.includes(item.scope) && safeText(item.observedAt, 80) && freshness.includes(item.freshness) && (item.freshnessRule === undefined || safeText(item.freshnessRule)) && (item.freshness === \"unknown\" || safeText(item.freshnessRule)) && (item.sourceVersion === undefined || safeSourceVersion(item.sourceVersion)) && trust.includes(item.trust) && safeText(item.retention) && safeText(item.inclusionReason) && safeText(item.retrievalMethod, 100) && Number.isFinite(item.estimatedTokens) && item.estimatedTokens >= 0 && (item.sourceRefs === undefined || (Array.isArray(item.sourceRefs) && item.sourceRefs.length <= 100 && item.sourceRefs.every((ref) => safeText(ref, 200))))) &&\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:570:  dimension: \"navigability\" | \"retrieval_speed\" | \"freshness\" | \"compounding_value\";\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:598:  const allFreshnessKnown = inventoryExists && snapshot.items.every((item) => item.freshness !== \"unknown\");\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:629:        dimension: \"freshness\", level: inventoryExists ? allFreshnessKnown ? 2 : 1 : null,\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:631:          { reference: \"cli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:ContextFreshness\", finding: `${snapshot.items.filter((item) => item.freshness === \"unknown\").length} item(s) have unknown freshness; no current-state claim is inferred from persistence.`, status: \"observed\" },\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:634:        unmetCriteria: [\"Per-source freshness identities for external inputs, tool policy, and individual memory provenance.\", \"A freshness objective backed by observed change-to-invalidation latency.\"],\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:635:        knownLimitations: [\"The bounded candidate fingerprint covers repository candidate state only; ignored files and provider-side context are not fingerprinted. Session and archive facts remain unknown unless independently revalidated.\"],\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:636:        nextImprovement: \"Measure change-to-invalidation latency and add source-specific freshness identities for context outside the repository candidate.\",\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:664:    ...(snapshot.workspaceState ? [`Workspace freshness: ${snapshot.workspaceState.comparison}; ${snapshot.workspaceState.invalidatedRepositoryItemIds.length} prior repository item(s) invalidated`] : []),\ncli/src/core/context_inventory.ts:669:    ...snapshot.items.map((item) => `${item.id} ${item.sourceType} @ ${item.sourceLocation} [${item.scope}; ${item.freshness}${item.freshnessRule ? ` (${item.freshnessRule})` : \"\"}${item.sourceVersion ? `; source-version=${encodeURIComponent(item.sourceVersion)}` : \"\"}; ${item.trust}] ${item.estimatedTokens} est. tokens; via ${item.retrievalMethod}`),\ncli/src/core/checkout_trust.ts:106:export function verifyCheckout(cwd: string): { reason?: string; gitDir?: string; workTree?: string } {\ncli/src/core/checkout_trust.ts:183:/** The reason `cwd` is not a trusted checkout (see `verifyCheckout`), or undefined. */\ncli/src/core/checkout_trust.ts:185:  return verifyCheckout(cwd).reason;\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:10:import { verifyCheckout } from \"./checkout_trust.js\";\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:425:export function computeCandidateIdentitySync(\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:429:  return computeCandidateIdentitySyncForTesting(workspacePath, options, fs);\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:432:/** Test seam for deterministic filesystem race fixtures; production callers use computeCandidateIdentitySync. */\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:433:export function computeCandidateIdentitySyncForTesting(\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:483:  const untrusted = verifyCheckout(workspacePath).reason;\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:979:  public computeCandidateIdentitySync(\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:983:    const identity = computeCandidateIdentitySync(workspacePath, options);\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:995:    return this.computeCandidateIdentitySync(workspacePath, options);\ncli/src/core/candidate.ts:1170:      currentIdentity = this.computeCandidateIdentitySync(workspacePath, options);\n## codex/context-maturity-v130...origin/release/v1.3.0 [ahead 41, behind 9]\n?? .cargo-target-context-maturity/\n?? cli/.local/\nccf7ef4611bf922b249883b38ea53e5964ca273e\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":803331508}},"started_at_ms":1795502131771,"completed_at_ms":1795502132575}}
