{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:35:46.667Z","ordinal":107903,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c42-e8d0-7ec1-8d46-757074eef47b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-22466885-1834-4c0a-8584-a8a9e4afeecc","process_id":"83459","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/771/comments --jq '.[] | [.user.login,.created_at,(.body|.[0:1100])] | @tsv' | tail -n 10"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh api repos/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/771/comments --jq '.[] | [.user.login,.created_at,(.body|.[0:1100])] | @tsv' | tail -n 10"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"coderabbitai[bot]\t2026-11-24T05:42:32Z\t<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> ## Review skipped\\n> \\n> Auto reviews are disabled on base/target branches other than the default branch.\\n> \\n> \\n> \\n> Please check the settings in the CodeRabbit UI or the `.coderabbit.yaml` file in this repository. To trigger a single review, invoke the `@coderabbitai review` command.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> <br>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - \nmikeholownych\t2026-11-24T05:59:06Z\t**Independent review at `7e58def9d65db39a24d5fe24bf9d32a0c85f50fc` — REQUEST CHANGES. The head has moved to `c615f6a1`, which changes four lines in two test files (the expectations of item 1) and no source, so item 2 applies to it unchanged.**\\n\\n**Blocking**\\n\\n1. **Two test files failed at `7e58def9` and pass on the base**: `audit_export` (17 pass, 2 fail: the warning text at line 142, and 11 files expected where there are now 12 at line 525) and `audit_command` (6 pass, 2 fail: `files: 11`, and the `--json` schema test). `c615f6a1` updates those expectations; CI on that head will show whether it is complete.\\n\\n2. **`nexus audit export` now runs git in a directory taken from recorded state without neutralising filters, and a clean filter there executes** (confirmed by running). `verifyCheckout` returns trusted for a plain repository with a `.git` directory. With `* filter=x` in `.gitattributes` and a `filter.x.clean` command in that repository's `.git/config`, calling `computeCandidateIdentitySync` with this PR's bounds ran the command twice (it wrote the marker file). `candidate.ts` ru\nmikeholownych\t2026-11-24T06:18:07Z\t**Re-review at `64a3b05302bc465882c092f279702290877c2a14` — REQUEST CHANGES. The head is now `3455d3f4`, which changes two lines of `audit_command.test.ts` and nothing else; everything about the source below applies to it.**\\n\\n**The blocker is not addressed.** Every commit since `7e58def9` touches test expectations only. `cli/src/core/candidate.ts` and `cli/src/audit_export.ts` are unchanged, and so is `docs/AUDIT.md`. Please do not merge this on green checks: the checks do not exercise a hostile workspace.\\n\\n**Programs configured in the workspace still run during `audit export`.** Each case below was run against both `computeCandidateIdentitySync` and the in-process `exportAuditBundle` with a seeded subject, on a throwaway repository whose tracked file had its mtime bumped so git had to re-hash it. \"Executed\" means the configured command wrote its marker file.\\n\\n| Vector | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| `filter.<x>.clean` via `.gitattributes` | executed |\\n| `filter.<x>.process` | executed (the export then reported `unavailable`) |\\n| `core.fsmonitor=<command>` | executed |\\n| `include.path` to a f\nmikeholownych\t2026-11-24T06:28:38Z\tThe blocker has a fix ready as a PR into this branch: #772 (\"do not hash a repository whose own Git configuration names a program\"). It adds a check in `audit_export.ts` before the candidate identity is computed and a test with five planted configurations; it does not touch `candidate.ts`, so receipt digests are unchanged. Merge it here, or reimplement it differently, and I will re-review. The newest commit here (`403f197d`) still changes test expectations only.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":204655440}},"started_at_ms":1795502145461,"completed_at_ms":1795502146666}}
