{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:41:01.928Z","ordinal":108019,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-4a1a3747-6cc1-4dba-980f-532d2dc58f24","process_id":"16985","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '220,320p' cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts; sed -n '390,450p' cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts; sed -n '1850,1905p' cli/src/agent.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '220,320p' cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts","name":"workspace_commands.ts","path":"cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '390,450p' cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts","name":"workspace_commands.ts","path":"cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1850,1905p' cli/src/agent.ts","name":"agent.ts","path":"cli/src/agent.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"      (command) => bridge.executeTool(\"run_command\", { command, timeout_secs: timeoutSecs }),\n      testCommand,\n    );\n  } finally {\n    bridge.setTurnSignal(undefined);\n  }\n  const lines = [`$ ${result.command}`, result.success ? \"Test suite passed.\" : \"Test suite failed.\"];\n  if (!result.success && result.failures.length) lines.push(\"\", \"Failing tests:\", ...result.failures.slice(0, 10).map((f) => `  • ${f}`));\n  if (!result.success && result.diagnostics.length) {\n    lines.push(\"\", \"Diagnostics:\", ...result.diagnostics.slice(0, 5).map((d) => `  • [${d.severity.toUpperCase()}] ${d.file || \"unknown\"}:${d.line || \"?\"} ${d.message}`));\n  }\n  return reply(\"test\", lines.join(\"\\n\"), result.success);\n}\n\nfunction lastAssistant(ctx: SlashContext): string {\n  const messages = ctx.host.app.getAgent().getMessages();\n  for (let i = messages.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n    const content = messages[i].content;\n    if (messages[i].role === \"assistant\" && content) return typeof content === \"string\" ? content : JSON.stringify(content);\n  }\n  return \"\";\n}\n\n/** The sanitised form of a copy, or nothing when the sanitiser failed (it returns a placeholder then). */\nexport function sanitizeForTerminal(text: string): string {\n  const safe = formatSafeSidecarText(text);\n  return safe === SANITIZATION_FAILED ? \"\" : safe;\n}\n\nfunction copy(ctx: SlashContext): SlashOutcome {\n  const what = ctx.args.trim().toLowerCase() || \"last\";\n  let text: string;\n  let label: string;\n  if (what === \"diff\") {\n    const cwd = workspace(ctx);\n    { const info = getGitInfo(cwd); if (!info.isRepo) return reply(\"copy\", info.refusal ?? NOT_A_REPO, false); }\n    text = git(cwd, [\"diff\"]);\n    if (!text.trim()) return reply(\"copy\", \"No uncommitted changes to copy.\", false);\n    label = `the git diff (${text.split(\"\\n\").length} lines)`;\n  } else {\n    const last = lastAssistant(ctx);\n    if (!last) return reply(\"copy\", \"No assistant reply to copy yet.\", false);\n    const blocks = what === \"code\" ? [...last.matchAll(/```[a-zA-Z0-9_-]*\\n([\\s\\S]*?)```/g)].map((m) => m[1].trimEnd()) : [];\n    text = blocks.length ? blocks.join(\"\\n\\n// ────────────────────────────\\n\\n\") : last;\n    label = blocks.length ? `${blocks.length} code block(s)` : `the last reply (${last.length} chars)`;\n  }\n  const result = copyWithFallback(text, process.env, sanitizeForTerminal);\n  if (!result.success) return reply(\"copy\", `Clipboard error: ${result.error}`, false);\n  if (result.osc52 !== undefined) {\n    return reply(\n      \"copy\",\n      `No clipboard tool was found, so Nexus asked your terminal to copy ${label} (OSC 52, ${Buffer.byteLength(result.osc52, \"utf8\")} bytes). ` +\n        \"Nexus cannot confirm it: if nothing arrived, the terminal ignores OSC 52 (tmux needs `set -g set-clipboard on`; GNU screen is not supported). \" +\n        \"Credential-looking text and control characters in it are replaced, as in /paste. NEXUS_OSC52=off turns this fallback off.\",\n      true,\n      { clipboard: result.osc52 },\n    );\n  }\n  return reply(\"copy\", `Copied ${label} to the clipboard.`);\n}\n\nfunction paste(): SlashOutcome {\n  const result = readFromClipboard();\n  if (!result.success || !result.text) return reply(\"paste\", `Clipboard error: ${result.error || \"the clipboard is empty\"}`, false);\n  if (result.text.length > MAX_PASTE) return reply(\"paste\", `The clipboard holds ${result.text.length} characters; /paste takes at most ${MAX_PASTE}.`, false);\n  return reply(\"paste\", `Pasted ${result.text.length} characters into the composer.`, true, { composer: result.text });\n}\n\nconst DEFAULT_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS = 2_000;\nconst MAX_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS = 30_000;\nconst MAX_CONTEXT_ITEMS = 500;\n\nasync function context({ host, args, signal }: SlashContext): Promise<SlashOutcome> {\n  const [view, ...tokens] = args.trim().split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n  const usage = \"Usage: /context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>] | /context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]\";\n  if (!view || ![\"inspect\", \"maturity\"].includes(view)) return reply(\"context\", usage, false);\n  let json = false;\n  let record = false;\n  let budgetMs = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS;\n  let maxItems = MAX_CONTEXT_ITEMS;\n  const seen = new Set<string>();\n  for (let index = 0; index < tokens.length; index++) {\n    const token = tokens[index];\n    if (seen.has(token)) return reply(\"context\", `Duplicate option: ${token}. ${usage}`, false);\n    seen.add(token);\n    if (token === \"--json\") { json = true; continue; }\n    if (token === \"--record\" && view === \"inspect\") { record = true; continue; }\n    if (token === \"--budget-ms\" || token === \"--max-items\") {\n      const value = tokens[++index];\n      if (!value || !/^[1-9]\\d*$/.test(value)) return reply(\"context\", `Invalid value for ${token}. ${usage}`, false);\n      const parsed = Number(value);\n      const upper = token === \"--budget-ms\" ? MAX_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS : MAX_CONTEXT_ITEMS;\n      if (!Number.isSafeInteger(parsed) || parsed > upper) return reply(\"context\", `Value for ${token} must be between 1 and ${upper}.`, false);\n      if (token === \"--budget-ms\") budgetMs = parsed;\n      else maxItems = parsed;\n      continue;\n    }\n    return reply(\"context\", `Invalid option: ${token}. ${usage}`, false);\n  }\n  if (signal.aborted) return reply(\"context\", \"Context inspection was cancelled.\", false);\n\n      if (timeout) clearTimeout(timeout);\n      if (abortListener) signal.removeEventListener(\"abort\", abortListener);\n    }\n  };\n\n  let promptComponentsAvailable = false;\n  await measure(\"system_prompt_components\", () => {\n    if (typeof agent.getSystemPromptContextSources !== \"function\") throw new Error(\"system prompt source API unavailable\");\n    const components = agent.getSystemPromptContextSources();\n    if (!components?.length) throw new Error(\"active system prompt source references are unavailable or stale\");\n    promptComponentsAvailable = true;\n    return components;\n  }, \"partial\", \"content is sliced from the active prompt in memory for token estimation; only metadata and source references are retained\");\n  if (!promptComponentsAvailable) gaps.push(\"active system prompt sections could not be linked to the current message; the transcript fallback is retained as one opaque item\");\n  await measure(\"session_messages\", (itemBudget) => {\n    const messages: any = agent.getMessages();\n    const collect = (value: any[]) => inventorySourcesFromMessagesBounded(\n      promptComponentsAvailable ? value.filter((message: any, index: number) => !(index === 0 && message?.role === \"system\")) : value,\n      { maxItems: itemBudget },\n    );\n    return messages && typeof messages.then === \"function\" ? messages.then(collect) : collect(messages);\n  });\n  let workspaceFingerprint: string | undefined;\n  await measure(\"workspace_state_fingerprint\", () => {\n    if (typeof agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint !== \"function\") throw new Error(\"workspace fingerprint API unavailable\");\n    workspaceFingerprint = agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint();\n    if (!workspaceFingerprint) throw new Error(\"workspace fingerprint unavailable\");\n    return [{\n      sourceType: \"workspace_state_fingerprint\",\n      sourceLocation: \"repository:candidate-identity\",\n      scope: \"repository\",\n      content: \"bounded composite candidate identity\",\n      trust: \"tool_output_unverified\",\n      retention: \"session_context_inventory\",\n      inclusionReason: \"supports equality comparison with the previous recorded workspace state; it is not evidence that repository content is correct\",\n      retrievalMethod: \"candidate_identity\",\n      freshness: \"current\",\n      freshnessRule: \"computed at capture from current candidate identity; any workspace candidate change invalidates this observation\",\n    }];\n  });\n  if (typeof agent.getInferenceContextManifests === \"function\") {\n    await measure(\"inference_request_manifests\", () => agent.getInferenceContextManifests().map((manifest: any) => ({\n        sourceType: \"inference_request_manifest\",\n        sourceLocation: `task:inference-request:${manifest.id}`,\n        scope: \"task\" as const,\n        content: JSON.stringify({ sequence: manifest.sequence, capturedAt: manifest.capturedAt, status: manifest.status, coverage: manifest.coverage, messageCount: manifest.messages.length, toolCount: manifest.tools.count, requestEstimateTokens: manifest.budget.requestEstimateTokens }),\n        trust: \"persisted_unverified\" as const,\n        retention: \"bounded_latest_24_session_records\",\n        inclusionReason: \"client-side record of message and tool-schema arrays handed to the adapter; dispatch status does not prove provider processing\",\n        retrievalMethod: \"agent_submit_wrapper\",\n        sourceRefs: manifest.messages.slice(0, 100).map((item: any) => item.sourceRef),\n      })));\n  } else {\n    await measure(\"inference_request_manifests\", () => [], \"partial\", \"request manifest history is unavailable from this agent instance\");\n  }\n  await measure(\"task_ledger\", () => {\n    const objective = agent.getObjective();\n    if (!objective) return [];\n    return [{ sourceType: \"objective_ledger\", sourceLocation: \"task:objective-ledger\", scope: \"task\", content: JSON.stringify(objective), trust: \"persisted_unverified\", retention: \"task\", inclusionReason: \"pinned objective and acceptance state\", retrievalMethod: \"durable_task_state\", freshness: \"current\", freshnessRule: \"read from the live task ledger at inspection time\", sourceRefs: objective.requirements?.map((requirement) => `requirement:${requirement.id}`) }];\n  });\n  await measure(\"plan\", () => {\n    if (this.hasPendingModifications) this.verificationEvidence = undefined;\n  }\n\n  public getHistoryCount(): number {\n    return this.messages.length;\n  }\n\n  public getUi(): TerminalUI {\n    return this.ui;\n  }\n\n  public setObserver(observer: AgentObserver | undefined): void {\n    this.observer = observer;\n  }\n\n  public getCompletionSummary(): { summary: string; notes?: string } | undefined {\n    return this.completionSummary;\n  }\n\n  public getConfig(): HarnessConfig {\n    return this.config;\n  }\n\n  public getWorkspacePathIdentity(): WorkspacePath {\n    return this.workspacePathIdentity;\n  }\n\n  /** A bounded, content-free candidate identity for revalidating recorded repository context. */\n  public getWorkspaceContextFingerprint(): string | undefined {\n    try {\n      return computeCandidateIdentitySync(this.config.workspace, { maxEntries: 4096, maxTotalBytes: 16 * 1024 * 1024 }).candidateId;\n    } catch {\n      // Unknown is safer than presenting an old repository observation as current.\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /** Judges, once per workspace, whether the session STARTED in a linked worktree the agent had already worked in. */\n  private judgeReceiptBaselineOnce(): void {\n    if (this.receiptBaselineJudged) return;\n    this.receiptBaselineJudged = true;\n    this.receiptBaselineUntrusted = this.linkedWorktreeStartsDirty();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Whether the workspace is a linked worktree that either holds uncommitted work or cannot be certified (a nested\n   * repository, a hidden edit, a dirty submodule). Fails closed there; a plain checkout or a non-repository is \"no\".\n   */\n  private linkedWorktreeStartsDirty(): boolean {\n    const workspace = this.config.workspace;\n    if (verifyCheckout(workspace).reason) return true; // a tampered pointer or a planted repository: not a plain checkout\n    let real: string;\n    try { real = fs.realpathSync(workspace); } catch { return false; }\n    // A registered linked worktree whose `.git` entry is missing or replaced is not a plain checkout either.\n    if (!fs.existsSync(path.join(real, \".git\")) && replacedWorktreeReason(real)) return true;\n    let linked = false;\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":866005459}},"started_at_ms":1795502461061,"completed_at_ms":1795502461928}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:41:01.937Z","ordinal":108020,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d10e46a5-a4da-4687-9f8d-c1c33f0f6609","process_id":"49365","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md && sed -n '1,220p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,240p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md","name":"CONCURRENCY.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,220p' docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md","name":"XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md","path":"docs/XERJ_REFERENCE_CODING.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\nThese files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n\n| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cli/src/agent.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 11 | Claim required. Keep each change local to the line ranges the plan names. Rebase immediately before merge and re-run that slice's tests on the rebased snapshot. |\n| `cli/src/index.ts` | 01, 03, 04, 06, 08, 10, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-06 PR-6b (unified launcher) lands first.** Other plans add commands and flags afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tools.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 06, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-02 PR-2b (signal plumbing) lands before PLAN-03 PR-3c (`safeFetch`)**. |\n| `cli/src/sidecar.ts` | 01, 02, 03, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/doctor.ts` | 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 | Claim required. Each plan adds **new check functions** in separate blocks. Only PLAN-06 PR-6d changes existing checks. |\n| `cli/src/client.ts` | 03, 05, 08, 11 | Claim required. **PLAN-03 PR-3a (env layering) lands before any PLAN-05 slice.** |\n| `cli/src/repl.ts` | 01, 05, 08 | Claim required |\n| `cli/src/config.ts`, `security.ts`, `sandbox.ts`, `mcp.ts`, `plugins.ts` | 01, 03 | Claim required. PLAN-01 PR-1e and PLAN-03 must not run at the same time on `sandbox.ts` or `security.ts`. |\n| `cli/src/core/capabilities.ts` | 01, 02 | **PLAN-01 PR-1a (effect classes) lands first.** PLAN-02 PR-2c adds schema fields afterwards. |\n| `cli/src/tester.ts` | 01, 11 | **PLAN-01 PR-1c lands before PLAN-11 PR-11b/11c.** |\n| `cli/src/core/state.ts` | 04, 08 | **PLAN-08 PR-8a (HOME isolation) lands before everything.** |\n| `core/src/runner.rs`, `core/src/main.rs` | 01, 02, 06 | Claim required. The protocol version number is owned by PLAN-02 PR-2a. PLAN-06 PR-6c only reads it. |\n| `core/src/bin/nexus_tui/{live_state,live_view}.rs` | 01, 02 | Claim required |\n| `package.json`, `cli/package.json`, `core/Cargo.toml`, lockfiles | 01, 06, 07, 08 | **Only one agent at a time.** Version fields are written only by `scripts/sync-version.mjs`. Dependency changes are separate commits that touch only the lockfile and manifest. |\n| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\n| `cli/dist/**` | all, while tracked | Do not commit `cli/dist` from slices. PLAN-07 PR-7d untracks it (DEC-10). Until that merges, only the merging agent rebuilds and commits dist, in a final separate commit, after rebasing. |\n| `docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CLOUD_PROVIDERS.md`, `quickstart.md` | 05, 09 and doc tasks in every plan | Edit only the sections your slice changes. Hold a short `FILE_` claim. |\n\n### Ledger updates (`docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md`)\n\nA slice changes only the rows for its own requirement IDs: the status, test-reference and evidence cells, in place. It never reorders, adds or removes rows, and never edits another slice's rows. New requirements discovered during work go to §6, not into the ledger. Because rows are independent lines, git merges these edits cleanly. If a conflict appears anyway, resolve it row by row, keeping both changes.\n\n## 5. Commit and merge discipline\n\n1. Before **every** commit, compare `git rev-parse HEAD` with the commit you last made. Then run `git log <yours>..HEAD` on the branch. If anything foreign appears, stop and reconcile. Never commit generated artifacts (evidence, dist, lockfiles) over a branch that moved (lessons 2026-10-13).\n2. Commits are scoped to the slice. Do not reformat or clean up files outside the boundary.\n3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n\n## 6. Coordination records\n\n| Record | Where | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n\n## 7. Safe parallel lanes\n\nThe following groupings can run at the same time with no hot-file contention beyond §4 claims. They are listed by milestone.\n\n| Phase | Parallel lanes |\n|---|---|\n| M0 | (a) PLAN-08 PR-8a, which must merge first. Then in parallel: (b) PLAN-06 PR-6a, (c) PLAN-09 PR-9a. |\n| M1 | (a) PLAN-01 PR-1a → PR-1b → PR-1c (sequential, owns `capabilities.ts`, `agent.ts` dispatch). (b) PLAN-02 PR-2a (Rust only). (c) PLAN-03 PR-3a → PR-3b (config/egress). (d) PLAN-11 PR-11a (`parser.ts`) and PR-11b (`tester.ts`, after PR-1c). Lanes (b), (c) and (d) do not touch `capabilities.ts`. |\n| M2 (alongside M1) | (a) PLAN-07 PR-7a/7b/7c (workflows, scripts). (b) PLAN-06 PR-6b after PLAN-01 PR-1b (shares `index.ts` flags). |\n| M3 | (a) PLAN-04 (`agent.ts` turn, operation runner). (b) PLAN-05 (`client.ts`, provider modules). (c) PLAN-10 harness (`eval/`, no product files). (d) Held-out task authoring by the agent author, **outside the repository**: no access to Nexus source or the development set (DEC-05). |\n| M4 (alongside M3) | PLAN-08 PR-8b..8e. Coordinate with PLAN-04 on `state.ts` through `FILE_` claims. |\n| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\n\n## 8. Independence constraints\n\n- The held-out task author must not see Nexus source, the development tasks or tuning history. It runs in a separate session with only the task schema and external repositories. Its output is sealed by a sha256 manifest committed before RC1.\n- The independent reviewer in ACCEPTANCE §8 must not be the agent or session that implemented the slices under review.\n- An implementing agent never edits `eval/heldout-manifest.json`, scorer thresholds or ACCEPTANCE §6.4 after the freeze.\n# Reference coding with XERJ\n\nThe detail behind the \"Reference coding\" rule in `AGENTS.md`: how to reach the local XERJ node, what to query, and what to leave alone.\n\n- Before non-trivial code with a peer-project analogue (feature, protocol, parser, worktree or provider handling, tool, test harness), query the local XERJ node and record what you took, borrowed or rejected in the PR's \"Reference coding\" section. Exempt: trivial edits, doc-only changes, fixes fully specified by a failing test.\n- XERJ is an owner-host tool, not a project dependency (`docs/v1.1.0/DECISIONS.md` §1). Where it is unavailable (contributor machine, CI), write \"XERJ unavailable: <reason>\" in that section and use `git grep` plus the peer's public source.\n- The node is the user service `xerj` on `http://localhost:9200`; confirm with `systemctl --user is-active xerj` and use that node. Stop a hub with `xerj hub stop`.\n- Corpora: `xerj corpus list`. Retrieval is lexical (BM25), so query with identifiers and words from the code: `xerj code <corpus> \"<words>\" -k 4 --full 600`, `xerj search --prefix <index-prefix> \"<words>\" -k 4`, `xerj def --prefix <prefix> \"<symbol>\"`. The first query can take over a minute; set a timeout.\n- `nexus-cli`, `nexus-core`, `nexus-test`, `nexus-docs` index `origin/main` only (hourly), so open PRs are absent: use `git grep` on your branch.\n- Reference code is read-only inspiration. Follow each result's licence tag; copy verbatim only permissively licensed code, with a citation. Keep XERJ and reference corpora away from held-out evaluation tasks (`docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md`). Keep document text local (`rerank` sends it to a third party). Leave indices you did not create alone.\n- After real use: `xerj feedback --dry-run`, then `xerj feedback --submit --agent \"<model>\" --used-for \"<task>\" --verdict \"<what worked and what did not>\"`, with secrets and private data left out.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":878711686}},"started_at_ms":1795502461055,"completed_at_ms":1795502461934}}
