{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:50:25.295Z","ordinal":108340,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0533afaf0c87d2b50caf0fbb8ea369","status":"completed","call_id":"call_3cc99db3899e4e83b99df0a9dbadc65e","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"rg -n \\\"candidate fingerprint|workspace fingerprint|Security|Limitation|Tests|Verification|Reference coding|Decision|Implemented\\\" docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1600}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","create_time":1795503023.6856468}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":48707,"sampled_through_sequence":48705,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:50:25.316Z","ordinal":108341,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","response_id":"resp_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0533ab1dbc87d29e280f692525f16f","usage":{"input_tokens":116063,"cached_input_tokens":115072,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":309,"reasoning_output_tokens":211,"total_tokens":116372},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":3952510,"cached_input_tokens":3867648,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":24008,"reasoning_output_tokens":12463,"total_tokens":3976518},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2325146960,"cached_input_tokens":2306850816,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3822085,"reasoning_output_tokens":1837857,"total_tokens":2328969045}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:50:26.256Z","ordinal":108342,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-287129f3-2438-45be-8c8e-4342e6d09fbc","process_id":"9554","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"candidate fingerprint|workspace fingerprint|Security|Limitation|Tests|Verification|Reference coding|Decision|Implemented\" docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'candidate fingerprint|workspace fingerprint|Security|Limitation|Tests|Verification|Reference coding|Decision|Implemented' docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md","query":"candidate fingerprint|workspace fingerprint|Security|Limitation|Tests|Verification|Reference coding|Decision|Implemented","path":"CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"18:## Implemented assessment\n26:| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Items carry explicit `current` / `stale` / `unknown` plus invalidation rules. Session and archive reconstruction marks history unknown. `/context inspect` records a bounded composite candidate fingerprint and compares it with the previous saved inventory; changed workspaces produce invalidated repository-item references and an explicit partial-coverage reason. Durable knowledge entries now explicitly report unknown freshness in inspection and prompt text because their opaque source references have no stored fingerprint or revalidation. | There is no per-source freshness identity for ignored environment inputs, tool policy, or individual memory provenance, and no measured change-to-invalidation objective. Memory freshness remains unknown; the system does not infer staleness or correctness from an opaque reference. |\n33:### Decision\n40:- `ContextInventorySnapshot`: schema version, capture time, session/task/workspace identity, optional bounded composite workspace fingerprint and comparison outcome, item list, per-source timing/status/counts, estimate provenance, omissions, completeness, and reason for incomplete or unknown coverage. Timeout/cancellation is an additive `outcome` value while the existing `status` remains `failed`, so schema-1 readers continue to accept the inventory.\n50:- No secret-bearing source text or per-file content hashes are copied into the inventory or maturity report. A composite candidate fingerprint supports equality comparison within the saved session; it does not reveal a file path or claim correctness. Paths are workspace-relative where possible. Inventory snapshots follow the containing session's existing retention/deletion behavior; no cross-user cache is introduced.\n59:2. Inventory content contains no source plaintext and distinguishes operator, model, tool, and persisted-knowledge trust states. A non-unknown freshness claim requires an explicit invalidation rule; persistence or resume without revalidation demotes `current` to `unknown`. A bounded current candidate fingerprint is compared with the previous capture; changed state reports prior repository-scoped references as invalidated, while missing fingerprints remain unknown.\n69:### Implemented boundary and deferred work\n75:## Reference coding\n79:## Verification evidence\n114:- Freshness compares bounded repository candidate fingerprints for saved session inventories, but does not cover ignored environment inputs, tool policy, provider-side context, or the underlying sources of individual memory claims. Memory freshness remains explicitly unknown; inventories now compare a bounded metadata version (record update timestamp plus validation status) and flag a prior captured record when either changes. That detects record mutation, not whether the remembered claim remains true. Invalidation latency has not been measured. The candidate scan is bounded by 4,096 manifest entries and 16 MiB of changed content, with Git's configured timeout; failures produce unknown freshness and partial coverage. No retrieval-latency SLO or cache instrumentation exists.\n184:After the full-suite run, `origin/release/v1.3.0` advanced to `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3` with inference-submission budgeting and protocol-schema updates. The context branch was rebased onto that tip; source-tested head is `8d4bb77a1bdb076012e510244f054bc9d4f943f4`. On that head, `make build` passed. Sequential isolated tests passed: `context_inventory.test.ts` 17/17, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` 3/3, `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` 90/90, `audit_export.test.ts` 18/18, and `session_durable_fields.test.ts` 4/4. The initial inventory attempt failed because this worktree's custom in-repository Cargo target contained an oversized generated `libgit2.a`, which the candidate fingerprint correctly rejected; after removing that task-generated directory and rerunning with the normal ignored build outputs, inventory passed 17/17. The evidence-only documentation commit followed that tested source head. The pre-rebase full-suite failure remains the latest full-run evidence and is not represented as qualification of `8d4bb77a`.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":704220214}},"started_at_ms":1795503025551,"completed_at_ms":1795503026256}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:50:26.394Z","ordinal":108343,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20c51-f0da-79b3-aa97-e4087141514e","call_id":"call_3cc99db3899e4e83b99df0a9dbadc65e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"18:## Implemented assessment\n26:| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Items carry explicit `current` / `stale` / `unknown` plus invalidation rules. Session and archive reconstruction marks history unknown. `/context inspect` records a bounded composite candidate fingerprint and compares it with the previous saved inventory; changed workspaces produce invalidated repository-item references and an explicit partial-coverage reason. Durable knowledge entries now explicitly report unknown freshness in inspection and prompt text because their opaque source references have no stored fingerprint or revalidation. | There is no per-source freshness identity for ignored environment inputs, tool policy, or individual memory provenance, and no measured change-to-invalidation objective. Memory freshness remains unknown; the system does not infer staleness or correctness from an opaque reference. |\n33:### Decision\n40:- `ContextInventorySnapshot`: schema version, capture time, session/task/workspace identity, optional bounded composite workspace fingerprint and comparison outcome, item list, per-source timing/status/counts, estimate provenance, omissions, completeness, and reason for incomplete or unknown coverage. Timeout/cancellation is an additive `outcome` value while the existing `status` remains `failed`, so schema-1 readers continue to accept the inventory.\n50:- No secret-bearing source text or per-file content hashes are copied into the inventory or maturity report. A composite candidate fingerprint supports equality comparison within the saved session; it does not reveal a file path or claim correctness. Paths are workspace-relative where possible. Inventory snapshots follow the containing session's existing retention/deletion behavior; no cross-user cache is introduced.\n59:2. Inventory content contains no source plaintext and distinguishes operator, model, tool, and persisted-knowledge trust states. A non-unknown freshness claim requires an explicit invalidation rule; persistence or resume without revalidation demotes `current` to `unknown`. A bounded current candidate fingerprint is compared with the previous capture; changed state reports prior repository-scoped references as invalidated, while missing fingerprints remain unknown.\n69:### Implemented boundary and deferred work\n75:## Reference coding\n79:## Verification evidence\n114:- Freshness compares bounded repository candidate fingerprints for saved session inventories, but does not cover ignored environment inputs, tool policy, provider-side context, or the underlying sources of individual memory claims. Memory freshness remains explicitly unknown; inventories now compare a bounded metadata version (record update timestamp plus validation status) and flag a prior captured record when either changes. That detects record mutation, not whether the remembered claim remains true. Invalidation latency has not been measured. The candidate scan is bounded by 4,096 manifest entries and 16 MiB of changed content, with Git's configured timeout; failures produce unknown freshness and partial coverage. No retrieval-latency SLO or cache instrumentation exists.\n184:After the full-suite run, `origin/release/v1.3.0` advanced to `51bf3db79fdadca26dbde6bbf752c9982c7793e3` with inference-submission budgeting and protocol-schema updates. The context branch was rebased onto that tip; source-tested head is `8d4bb77a1bdb076012e510244f054bc9d4f943f4`. On that head, `make build` passed. Sequential isolated tests passed: `context_inventory.test.ts` 17/17, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` 3/3, `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` 90/90, `audit_export.test.ts` 18/18, and `session_durable_fields.test.ts` 4/4. The initial inventory attempt failed because this worktree's custom in-repository Cargo target contained an oversized generated `libgit2.a`, which the candidate fingerprint correctly rejected; after removing that task-generated directory and rerunning with the normal ignored build outputs, inventory passed 17/17. The evidence-only documentation commit followed that tested source head. The pre-rebase full-suite failure remains the latest full-run evidence and is not represented as qualification of `8d4bb77a`.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","create_time":1795503026.3943012}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":48708,"sampled_through_sequence":48705,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
