ot a green full-suite result.\n\nThe cancellation test was then run five times sequentially with isolated `HOME` and ephemeral mock-provider ports; all five passed in 137–147 ms. Source inspection confirms the caller signal is wired into `StreamWatchdog`, which aborts the fetch signal, and `readSse` cancels its reader on error. These repeats do not explain the full-shard timeout, so the intermittent failure remains unresolved and must not be classified as environmental or fixed. On the subsequently rebased current source, focused tests passed: `context_inventory.test.ts` 17/17, `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` 3/3, `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` (all cases passed), session persistence/export/fork test files (all passed), and `audit_export.test.ts` 18/18. `make build` also passed with isolated `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, and a worktree-local `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`.\n\nThis rebase includes release-branch commits not present in the full-suite snapshot; full-suite status at the exact current head is therefore unverified. The four maturity ratings…805 tokens truncated…cal materialized mode was restored to `0644` and the timeout was raised to 900 seconds; no tracked source was changed. The evaluator and long-file cases were rerun, then the complete `make test` was executed serially under the SUITE claim with isolated HOME, worktree-local Cargo output, and unique temporary fixture roots.\n\nResults from the corrected run: Rust core tests passed 53/53, Rust TUI tests passed 406/406, and the remaining Rust integration groups passed 9/9. The CLI suite reported 3,053 tests: 3,052 passed, 0 failed, and 1 skipped. Terminal acceptance reported 3,111 tests: 3,095 passed, 0 failed, and 16 skipped. The terminal scope fixtures passed. Every lifecycle security gate reported success, including Node and Rust dependency audits, credential scanning, diff hygiene, and forbidden-documentation scanning. The run output contained no Makefile `[!] FAILED` step marker or final `make test: one or more steps failed` message.\n\nThe outer validation command nevertheless returned exit code 1 after the security gates printed success, with `zsh:42: PIPESTATUS[0]: parameter not set`. Thus the component summaries are green, but the aggregate shell-wrapper status was not captured cleanly; this record does not label the aggregate command as a verified exit-0 run. The exact command output is retained at `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-2b623b44-fixed.log`. The command's own evaluator tmpfs and runtime roots were removed after its process exited; the separate isolated HOME is retained for diagnostics. The owner checkout and the shared fixture paths were not modified.\n\nThese results supersede the older predecessor-only suite reports as the most recent full-suite evidence, but establish local component qualification only. The maturity ratings remain Navigability 2 — Exploratory, Retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, Freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and Compounding value 1 in the no-memory fixture / 2 only when durable context is observed. There is still no held-out evidence that durable memory improves task outcomes, no measured retrieval SLO or end-to-end latency distribution, and durable-memory freshness remains unknown where source fingerprints are unavailable. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a fresh full run whose outer command exits zero remain outstanding. No inference provider was modified, and no push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n\n### Validation update — 2026-11-24, current rebased release snapshot\n\nOn implementation head `52b54573264a1ac563119a9f318e57affc3a2753`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `d03e6199f37bd024f17a807f00ed261291f8a02c`, `make build` passed in an isolated snapshot. The subsequent exact-head `make test` completed its Rust and terminal-security stages but failed in the second CLI shard. Rust core passed 53/53, Rust TUI passed 406/406, and the other Rust integration groups passed (1/1, 3/3, 4/4, and 1/1); the first CLI shard reported 3,108/3,112 passed with 4 skipped. The second CLI shard reported 3,057 tests: 3,043 passed, 1 failed, and 13 skipped. Its sole failure was `test/turn_semantics.test.ts`, “the same trajectory with a passing verifier is VERIFIED only through the verifier run”: expected `execution === COMPLETED`, received `FAILED`. Terminal scope fixtures passed and all lifecycle security gates printed success, but `make test` ended with `make: *** [Makefile:67: test] Error 1`; this is a failed aggregate run.\n\nThe complete `turn_semantics.test.ts` file was then run alone on the same snapshot with an isolated HOME and passed 37/37 in 94.2 seconds. This non-reproduction does not erase the full-suite failure or establish its cause. The exact full-run log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-52b54573-built.log`. No source was changed during these runs. The release branch has since advanced beyond this tested base; the implementation must be rebased and requalified at its current tip before making a release-level claim. Hosted checks, installed acceptance, independent review, and a clean exact-current full-suite run remain outstanding. No live inference was used and no inference provider, PR, release tag, or remote branch was changed.\n\n### Validation update — 2026-11-24, corrected full suite on snapshot `7b04317a`\n\nThe exact tested commit was `7b04317ab34bacdbd4ccd29511aff25a7aa647f8`, whose release base was `2dea217937aa7b49a0719b4bbfe3d9a9f9658acd`. A detached snapshot was built successfully with `make build`, an isolated HOME, and worktree-local build outputs. The first suite attempt on this snapshot had evaluator preflight failures because the checkout materialized `eval/scan-compiler-exposure.mjs` as group-writable even though Git records mode `100644`; the corrected snapshot restored the physical mode to `0644` without changing tracked files. The corrected `make test` used `NEXUS_TEST_FILE_TIMEOUT_SECS=900` for the existing long integration files and exited 0.\n\nResults: Rust core 53/53, Rust TUI 406/406, other Rust integration groups 9/9; CLI shards 2,724 tests (2,722 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped) and 3,452 tests (3,437 passed, 0 failed, 15 skipped), totaling 6,176 CLI tests (6,159 passed, 0 failed, 17 skipped). Terminal scope measurement fixtures passed. All lifecycle security gates passed, including Node/Rust dependency checks, credential scanning, diff hygiene, and documentation scanning. The two CLI shard fixture failures visible in the log are the intentional failing-child cases exercised by `test_shards.test.ts`; the shard test suite itself passed. The exact log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-7b04317a-fixed.log`; the command reported `MAKE_TEST_EXIT=0`. The isolated HOME is retained for diagnostics, and the run's unique evaluator mount/runtime paths were removed.\n\nThis result supersedes the earlier failed run on `52b54573` as the newest complete local full-suite result, but it qualifies only commit `7b04317a` and its `2dea2179` release base. `origin/release/v1.3.0` has since advanced to `5abbc4cbb24a2601b8b1c70acc908a90f73926df`; the implementation still needs rebasing and exact-current requalification. These are local tests, not hosted checks or installed acceptance. The maturity ratings do not change: Navigability 2 — Exploratory, Retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, Freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and Compounding value 1 in the no-memory fixture / 2 only when durable context is observed. Held-out evidence of memory value, a measured retrieval SLO, independent review, and installed acceptance remain outstanding. No inference-provider modification or live inference was used; no push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","create_time":1795503091.8653276}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":48731,"sampled_through_sequence":48728,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
