{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:51:49.809Z","ordinal":108401,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-8bea47af-e46b-48b2-9871-8a466c9f38bc","changes":{"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -50,2 +50,3 @@\n - No secret-bearing source text or per-file content hashes are copied into the inventory or maturity report. A composite candidate fingerprint supports equality comparison within the saved session; it does not reveal a file path or claim correctness. Paths are workspace-relative where possible. Inventory snapshots follow the containing session's existing retention/deletion behavior; no cross-user cache is introduced.\n+- Context freshness fingerprinting first performs filesystem-only inspection of repository, worktree, system, and global Git configuration. Command-bearing filter, fsmonitor, external-diff, credential-helper, and related settings; included configuration; malformed configuration; or an unreadable configuration prevent Git fingerprint commands from running. The inventory reports a failed source measurement, partial coverage, and unknown freshness with a bounded reason. This is a conservative context-diagnostic guard, not a general Git sandbox; other Git callers retain their own execution-boundary requirements.\n - Workspace changes do not silently make an old observation current. If Nexus has no compatible source fingerprint, freshness remains `unknown`.\n@@ -78,2 +79,4 @@\n \n+For the Git-configuration safety follow-up, XERJ located OpenCode's managed-repository diff handling (`packages/core/src/git.ts:937`) and test setup for `core.fsmonitor` configuration (`packages/core/script/snapshot-parity.ts:22-44`). That code exercises repositories OpenCode creates or manages and does not provide a guard for arbitrary user workspaces. Nexus therefore uses a bounded, filesystem-only preflight and refuses to fingerprint when effective configuration sources cannot be inspected conservatively; it does not assume managed-repository settings make a user checkout safe.\n+\n ## Verification evidence\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1795503109807,"completed_at_ms":1795503109809}}
