ting. It fails closed for command-bearing settings, included configuration, unsupported syntax, config-count overrides, and inaccessible config. `AutonomousAgent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult()` preserves a typed unavailability reason while the previous string-returning accessor remains compatible (`cli/src/agent.ts:1878-1892`). `/context inspect` records a failed source measurement and an explicit unknown-freshness reason instead of recording a current fingerprint (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:293-310,426-451`). This guard applies to the context fingerprint caller; it is not a general sandbox for other Git operations.\n+\n+The adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. The isolated `context_inventory.test.ts` run passed 20/20; `npm run build` passed before the final fixture and common-config inspection adjustment, so build must be repeated. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. The source patch is on the implementation worktree and has not been rebased, committed, pushed, or independently reviewed; PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1795503125049,"completed_at_ms":1795503125051}}
