insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md b/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\nindex 58be4416..7fe40d10 100644\n--- a/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n+++ b/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ Add a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that\n - Existing message and session schemas remain readable. New metadata is additive and source-only; full message and tool content remains in the existing session/archive path.\n - Hashes and locators are diagnostic provenance, not proof that a tool observation is true. Model output is labeled model-generated; tool output is labeled unverified unless an existing verifier receipt binds it.\n - No secret-bearing source text or per-file content hashes are copied into the inventory or maturity report. A composite candidate fingerprint supports equality comparison within the saved session; it does not reveal a file path or claim correctness. Paths are workspace-relative where possible. Inventory snapshots follow the containing session's existing retention/deletion behavior; no cross-user cache is introduced.\n+- Context freshness fingerprinting first performs filesystem-only inspection of repository, worktree, system, and global Git configuration. Command-bearing filter, fsmonitor, external-diff, credential-helper, and related settings; included configuration; malformed configuration; or an unreadable configuration prevent Git fingerprint commands from running. The inventory reports a failed source measurement, partial coverage, and unknown freshness with a bounded reason. This is a conservative context-diagnostic guard, not a general Git sandbox; other Git callers retain their own execution-boundary requirements.\n - Workspace changes do not silently make an old observation current. If Nexus has no compatible source fingerprint, freshness remains `unknown`.\n - Inventory collection is local and read-only. Failed or unsupported sources are reported with explicit partial status.\n - Durable project knowledge is promoted only through explicit operator commands. Model-invoked `manage_knowledge` rejects `set` even through the internal handler, and the model-visible schema omits that action. Legacy conversation auto-extraction is a no-op, including when its old environment flag is present.\n@@ -76,6 +77,8 @@ Add a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that\n \n XERJ retrieval on `nexus-cli` located the existing context admission/token-accounting path in `cli/src/agent.ts` (`requestMessages`, `admitContext`), the `manage_knowledge` capability (`cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts:23`), the local project knowledge graph (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`), and `computeCandidateIdentitySync` (`cli/src/core/candidate.ts:425`, class method at line 979). The XERJ candidate lookup was lexical; direct branch inspection confirmed that the candidate identity includes the base commit and bounded changed workspace files. OpenCode transport code distinguishes request/read timeout failures and leaves the total-request budget opt-in (`packages/ai/src/route/transport/http.ts:108`); Nexus adopts an explicit caller-selected inspection budget and truthful timeout outcomes, without copying peer code. Nexus keeps the existing `KnowledgeGraph`, removes model-write affordances at both schema and handler, reuses candidate identity for freshness comparison, and rejects a second planner, provider-specific context protocol, external retrieval service, or copied peer implementation. XERJ indexes committed `origin/main`; the active worktree was checked directly.\n \n+For the Git-configuration safety follow-up, XERJ located OpenCode's managed-repository diff handling (`packages/core/src/git.ts:937`) and test setup for `core.fsmonitor` configuration (`packages/core/script/snapshot-parity.ts:22-44`). That code exercises repositories OpenCode creates or manages and does not provide a guard for arbitrary user workspaces. Nexus therefore uses a bounded, filesystem-only preflight and refuses to fingerprint when effective configuration sources cannot be inspected conservatively; it does not assume managed-repository settings make a user checkout safe.\n+\n ## Verification evidence\n \n Implementation worktree: `codex/context-maturity-v130`. The feature branch began from `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `a57c6c24` and was rebased onto the current release base `10942d410875f09e469cf7b39979cfa9c336974b`; changes remain local, with no push or PR publication.\n@@ -208,3 +211,11 @@ The exact tested commit was `7b04317ab34bacdbd4ccd29511aff25a7aa647f8`, whose re\n Results: Rust core 53/53, Rust TUI 406/406, other Rust integration groups 9/9; CLI shards 2,724 tests (2,722 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped) and 3,452 tests (3,437 passed, 0 failed, 15 skipped), totaling 6,176 CLI tests (6,159 passed, 0 failed, 17 skipped). Terminal scope measurement fixtures passed. All lifecycle security gates passed, including Node/Rust dependency checks, credential scanning, diff hygiene, and documentation scanning. The two CLI shard fixture failures visible in the log are the intentional failing-child cases exercised by `test_shards.test.ts`; the shard test suite itself passed. The exact log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-7b04317a-fixed.log`; the command reported `MAKE_TEST_EXIT=0`. The isolated HOME is retained for diagnostics, and the run's unique evaluator mount/runtime paths were removed.\n \n This result supersedes the earlier failed run on `52b54573` as the newest complete local full-suite result, but it qualifies only commit `7b04317a` and its `2dea2179` release base. `origin/release/v1.3.0` has since advanced to `5abbc4cbb24a2601b8b1c70acc908a90f73926df`; the implementation still needs rebasing and exact-current requalification. These are local tests, not hosted checks or installed acceptance. The maturity ratings do not change: Navigability 2 — Exploratory, Retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, Freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and Compounding value 1 in the no-memory fixture / 2 only when durable context is observed. Held-out evidence of memory value, a measured retrieval SLO, independent review, and installed acceptance remain outstanding. No inference-provider modification or live inference was used; no push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n+\n+### Security follow-up — workspace Git configuration during freshness capture\n+\n+Review of the context freshness path identified that `getWorkspaceContextFingerprint()` called `computeCandidateIdentitySync()` directly. Candidate identity uses Git commands, and repository or environment configuration can bind filters, fsmonitor, included configuration, or other program settings. Context inspection must not treat that risk as a documented limitation while still running those commands.\n+\n+`cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts` now uses bounded, non-following filesystem reads to inspect worktree metadata and repository, system, and global Git configuration before fingerprinting. It fails closed for command-bearing settings, included configuration, unsupported syntax, config-count overrides, and inaccessible config. `AutonomousAgent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult()` preserves a typed unavailability reason while the previous string-returning accessor remains compatible (`cli/src/agent.ts:1878-1892`). `/context inspect` records a failed source measurement and an explicit unknown-freshness reason instead of recording a current fingerprint (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:293-310,426-451`). This guard applies to the context fingerprint caller; it is not a general sandbox for other Git operations.\n+\n+The adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. On the current source changes, isolated `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 20/20 and `npm run build` passed. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. The source patch is on the implementation worktree and has not been rebased, committed, pushed, or independently reviewed; PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\ndiff --git a/cli/src/agent.ts b/cli/src/agent.ts\nindex 857f3374..3648fec9 100644\n--- a/cli/src/agent.ts\n+++ b/cli/src/agent.ts\n@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ import { captureVerificationState } from \"./worktrunk/verification.js\";\n import { homeDir } from \"./worktrunk/core.js\";\n import { openRepo, currentEntry, NotARepositoryError } from \"./worktrunk/repo.js\";\n import { replacedWorktreeReason, verifyCheckout } from \"./core/checkout_trust.js\";\n+import { inspectWorkspaceGitSafety, type WorkspaceGitSafetyReason } from \"./core/workspace_git_safety.js\";\n import { WORKTREE_BINDING_VERSION } from \"./core/state.js\";\n import { argsFingerprint } from \"./core/operation_identity.js\";\n import { isSandboxAvailable } from \"./sandbox.js\";\n@@ -1875,15 +1876,22 @@ export class AutonomousAgent {\n   }\n \n   /** A bounded, content-free candidate identity for revalidating recorded repository context. */\n-  public getWorkspaceContextFingerprint(): string | undefined {\n+  public getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult(): { fingerprint?: string; unavailableReason?: WorkspaceGitSafetyReason } {\n+    const safety = inspectWorkspaceGitSafety(this.config.workspace);\n+    if (!safety.safe) return { unavailableReason: safety.reason };\n     try {\n-      return computeCandidateIdentitySync(this.config.workspace, { maxEntries: 4096, maxTotalBytes: 16 * 1024 * 1024 }).candidateId;\n+      return { fingerprint: computeCandidateIdentitySync(this.config.workspace, { maxEntries: 4096, maxTotalBytes: 16 * 1024 * 1024 }).candidateId };\n     } catch {\n       // Unknown is safer than presenting an old repository observation as current.\n-      return undefined;\n+      return { unavailableReason: \"fingerprint_failed\" };\n     }\n   }\n \n+  /** Backward-compatible fingerprint accessor; callers needing an explanation use the result form. */\n+  public getWorkspaceContextFingerprint(): string | undefined {\n+    return this.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult().fingerprint;\n+  }\n+\n   /** Judges, once per workspace, whether the session STARTED in a linked worktree the agent had already worked in. */\n   private judgeReceiptBaselineOnce(): void {\n     if (this.receiptBaselineJudged) return;\ndiff --git a/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts b/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\nindex e36f2e3a..21ecf59a 100644\n--- a/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\n+++ b/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\n@@ -289,6 +289,20 @@ const DEFAULT_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS = 2_000;\n const MAX_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS = 30_000;\n const MAX_CONTEXT_ITEMS = 500;\n \n+class ContextSourceReadFailure extends Error {\n+  constructor(readonly safeDetail: string) { super(safeDetail); }\n+}\n+\n+function fingerprintUnavailableDetail(reason: string | undefined): string {\n+  switch (reason) {\n+    case \"program_settings_present\": return \"repository Git configuration contains program settings; fingerprinting was refused and freshness is unknown\";\n+    case \"configuration_unrecognized\": return \"repository Git configuration could not be safely interpreted; fingerprinting was refused and freshness is unknown\";\n+    case \"configuration_unavailable\": return \"repository Git configuration could not be inspected safely; fingerprinting was refused and freshness is unknown\";\n+    case \"fingerprint_failed\": return \"workspace fingerprint computation failed; freshness is unknown\";\n+    default: return \"workspace fingerprint API is unavailable; freshness is unknown\";\n+  }\n+}\n+\n async function context({ host, args, signal }: SlashContext): Promise<SlashOutcome> {\n   const [view, ...tokens] = args.trim().split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n   const usage = \"Usage: /context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>] | /context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]\";\n@@ -383,9 +397,10 @@ async function context({ host, args, signal }: SlashContext): Promise<SlashOutco\n         }\n         recordSourceItems(name, status, durationMs, result as SourceReadResult, detail);\n       }\n-    } catch {\n-      sources.push({ name, status: \"failed\", durationMs: performance.now() - started, items: [], detail: \"source lookup failed; no source content was recorded\" });\n-      gaps.push(`${name} source lookup failed`);\n+    } catch (error) {\n+      const detail = error instanceof ContextSourceReadFailure ? error.safeDetail : \"source lookup failed; no source content was recorded\";\n+      sources.push({ name, status: \"failed\", durationMs: performance.now() - started, items: [], detail });\n+      gaps.push(`${name} ${detail}`);\n     } finally {\n       if (timeout) clearTimeout(timeout);\n       if (abortListener) signal.removeEventListener(\"abort\", abortListener);\n@@ -411,9 +426,16 @@ async function context({ host, args, signal }: SlashContext): Promise<SlashOutco\n   });\n   let workspaceFingerprint: string | undefined;\n   await measure(\"workspace_state_fingerprint\", () => {\n-    if (typeof agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint !== \"function\") throw new Error(\"workspace fingerprint API unavailable\");\n-    workspaceFingerprint = agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint();\n-    if (!workspaceFingerprint) throw new Error(\"workspace fingerprint unavailable\");\n+    if (typeof agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult === \"function\") {\n+      const result = agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult();\n+      workspaceFingerprint = result.fingerprint;\n+      if (!workspaceFingerprint) throw new ContextSourceReadFailure(fingerprintUnavailableDetail(result.unavailableReason));\n+    } else if (typeof agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint === \"function\") {\n+      workspaceFingerprint = agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint();\n+      if (!workspaceFingerprint) throw new ContextSourceReadFailure(fingerprintUnavailableDetail(undefined));\n+    } else {\n+      throw new ContextSourceReadFailure(fingerprintUnavailableDetail(undefined));\n+    }\n     return [{\n       sourceType: \"workspace_state_fingerprint\",\n       sourceLocation: \"repository:candidate-identity\",\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":985561946}},"started_at_ms":1795503183453,"completed_at_ms":1795503184440}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T06:53:04.608Z","ordinal":108443,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20c54-5ae0-70a3-a8ab-cfaac9168add","call_id":"call_42723d67a97e4fd68664a3991fdb2772","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"ccf7ef4611bf922b249883b38ea53e5964ca273e\nccf7ef46 (HEAD -> codex/context-maturity-v130) docs(context): record exact full-suite success\n7b04317a docs(context): record current full suite failure\n25865593 docs(context): record corrected full suite evidence\n5ba43e84 docs(context): distinguish tested source head\na099eb7b docs(context): record latest rebase qualification\n M cli/src/agent.ts\n M cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\n M cli/test/context_inventory.test.ts\n M docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n?? .cargo-target-context-maturity/\n?? cli/.local/\n?? cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts\n cli/src/agent.ts                                   |  14 ++-\n cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts                |  34 +++++-\n cli/test/context_inventory.test.ts                 | 133 ++++++++++++++++++++-\n .../context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md |  11 ++\n 4 files changed, 179 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md b/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\nindex 58be4416..7fe40d10 100644\n--- a/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n+++ b/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\n@@ -48,6 +48,7 @@ Add a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that\n - Existing message and session schemas remain readable. New metadata is additive and source-only; full message and tool content remains in the existing session/archive path.\n - Hashes and locators are diagnostic provenance, not proof that a tool observation is true. Model output is labeled model-generated; tool output is labeled unverified unless an existing verifier receipt binds it.\n - No secret-bearing source text or per-file content hashes are copied into the inventory or maturity report. A composite candidate fingerprint supports equality comparison within the saved session; it does not reveal a file path or claim correctness. Paths are workspace-relative where possible. Inventory snapshots follow the containing session's existing retention/deletion behavior; no cross-user cache is introduced.\n+- Context freshness fingerprinting first performs filesystem-only inspection of repository, worktree, system, and global Git configuration. Command-bearing filter, fsmonitor, external-diff, credential-helper, and related settings; included configuration; malformed configuration; or an unreadable configuration prevent Git fingerprint commands from running. The inventory reports a failed source measurement, partial coverage, and unknown freshness with a bounded reason. This is a conservative context-diagnostic guard, not a general Git sandbox; other Git callers retain their own execution-boundary requirements.\n - Workspace changes do not silently make an old observation current. If Nexus has no compatible source fingerprint, freshness remains `unknown`.\n - Inventory collection is local and read-only. Failed or unsupported sources are reported with explicit partial status.\n - Durable project knowledge is promoted only through explicit operator commands. Model-invoked `manage_knowledge` rejects `set` even through the internal handler, and the model-visible schema omits that action. Legacy conversation auto-extraction is a no-op, including when its old environment flag is present.\n@@ -76,6 +77,8 @@ Add a small, local context inventory and deterministic maturity assessment that\n \n XERJ retrieval on `nexus-cli` located the existing context admission/token-accounting path in `cli/src/agent.ts` (`requestMessages`, `admitContext`), the `manage_knowledge` capability (`cli/src/core/capability_definitions/knowledge.ts:23`), the local project knowledge graph (`cli/src/knowledge.ts:37-45`), and `computeCandidateIdentitySync` (`cli/src/core/candidate.ts:425`, class method at line 979). The XERJ candidate lookup was lexical; direct branch inspection confirmed that the candidate identity includes the base commit and bounded changed workspace files. OpenCode transport code distinguishes request/read timeout failures and leaves the total-request budget opt-in (`packages/ai/src/route/transport/http.ts:108`); Nexus adopts an explicit caller-selected inspection budget and truthful timeout outcomes, without copying peer code. Nexus keeps the existing `KnowledgeGraph`, removes model-write affordances at both schema and handler, reuses candidate identity for freshness comparison, and rejects a second planner, provider-specific context protocol, external retrieval service, or copied peer implementation. XERJ indexes committed `origin/main`; the active worktree was checked directly.\n \n+For the Git-configuration safety follow-up, XERJ located OpenCode's managed-repository diff handling (`packages/core/src/git.ts:937`) and test setup for `core.fsmonitor` configuration (`packages/core/script/snapshot-parity.ts:22-44`). That code exercises repositories OpenCode creates or manages and does not provide a guard for arbitrary user workspaces. Nexus therefore uses a bounded, filesystem-only preflight and refuses to fingerprint when effective configuration sources cannot be inspected conservatively; it does not assume managed-repository settings make a user checkout safe.\n+\n ## Verification evidence\n \n Implementation worktree: `codex/context-maturity-v130`. The feature branch began from `origin/release/v1.3.0` at `a57c6c24` and was rebased onto the current release base `10942d410875f09e469cf7b39979cfa9c336974b`; changes remain local, with no push or PR publication.\n@@ -208,3 +211,11 @@ The exact tested commit was `7b04317ab34bacdbd4ccd29511aff25a7aa647f8`, whose re\n Results: Rust core 53/53, Rust TUI 406/406, other Rust integration groups 9/9; CLI shards 2,724 tests (2,722 passed, 0 failed, 2 skipped) and 3,452 tests (3,437 passed, 0 failed, 15 skipped), totaling 6,176 CLI tests (6,159 passed, 0 failed, 17 skipped). Terminal scope measurement fixtures passed. All lifecycle security gates passed, including Node/Rust dependency checks, credential scanning, diff hygiene, and documentation scanning. The two CLI shard fixture failures visible in the log are the intentional failing-child cases exercised by `test_shards.test.ts`; the shard test suite itself passed. The exact log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-7b04317a-fixed.log`; the command reported `MAKE_TEST_EXIT=0`. The isolated HOME is retained for diagnostics, and the run's unique evaluator mount/runtime paths were removed.\n \n This result supersedes the earlier failed run on `52b54573` as the newest complete local full-suite result, but it qualifies only commit `7b04317a` and its `2dea2179` release base. `origin/release/v1.3.0` has since advanced to `5abbc4cbb24a2601b8b1c70acc908a90f73926df`; the implementation still needs rebasing and exact-current requalification. These are local tests, not hosted checks or installed acceptance. The maturity ratings do not change: Navigability 2 — Exploratory, Retrieval speed 2 — Exploratory, Freshness 1 — Ad hoc, and Compounding value 1 in the no-memory fixture / 2 only when durable context is observed. Held-out evidence of memory value, a measured retrieval SLO, independent review, and installed acceptance remain outstanding. No inference-provider modification or live inference was used; no push, PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n+\n+### Security follow-up — workspace Git configuration during freshness capture\n+\n+Review of the context freshness path identified that `getWorkspaceContextFingerprint()` called `computeCandidateIdentitySync()` directly. Candidate identity uses Git commands, and repository or environment configuration can bind filters, fsmonitor, included configuration, or other program settings. Context inspection must not treat that risk as a documented limitation while still running those commands.\n+\n+`cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts` now uses bounded, non-following filesystem reads to inspect worktree metadata and repository, system, and global Git configuration before fingerprinting. It fails closed for command-bearing settings, included configuration, unsupported syntax, config-count overrides, and inaccessible config. `AutonomousAgent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult()` preserves a typed unavailability reason while the previous string-returning accessor remains compatible (`cli/src/agent.ts:1878-1892`). `/context inspect` records a failed source measurement and an explicit unknown-freshness reason instead of recording a current fingerprint (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:293-310,426-451`). This guard applies to the context fingerprint caller; it is not a general sandbox for other Git operations.\n+\n+The adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. On the current source changes, isolated `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 20/20 and `npm run build` passed. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. The source patch is on the implementation worktree and has not been rebased, committed, pushed, or independently reviewed; PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\ndiff --git a/cli/src/agent.ts b/cli/src/agent.ts\nindex 857f3374..3648fec9 100644\n--- a/cli/src/agent.ts\n+++ b/cli/src/agent.ts\n@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@ import { captureVerificationState } from \"./worktrunk/verification.js\";\n import { homeDir } from \"./worktrunk/core.js\";\n import { openRepo, currentEntry, NotARepositoryError } from \"./worktrunk/repo.js\";\n import { replacedWorktreeReason, verifyCheckout } from \"./core/checkout_trust.js\";\n+import { inspectWorkspaceGitSafety, type WorkspaceGitSafetyReason } from \"./core/workspace_git_safety.js\";\n import { WORKTREE_BINDING_VERSION } from \"./core/state.js\";\n import { argsFingerprint } from \"./core/operation_identity.js\";\n import { isSandboxAvailable } from \"./sandbox.js\";\n@@ -1875,15 +1876,22 @@ export class AutonomousAgent {\n   }\n \n   /** A bounded, content-free candidate identity for revalidating recorded repository context. */\n-  public getWorkspaceContextFingerprint(): string | undefined {\n+  public getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult(): { fingerprint?: string; unavailableReason?: WorkspaceGitSafetyReason } {\n+    const safety = inspectWorkspaceGitSafety(this.config.workspace);\n+    if (!safety.safe) return { unavailableReason: safety.reason };\n     try {\n-      return computeCandidateIdentitySync(this.config.workspace, { maxEntries: 4096, maxTotalBytes: 16 * 1024 * 1024 }).candidateId;\n+      return { fingerprint: computeCandidateIdentitySync(this.config.workspace, { maxEntries: 4096, maxTotalBytes: 16 * 1024 * 1024 }).candidateId };\n     } catch {\n       // Unknown is safer than presenting an old repository observation as current.\n-      return undefined;\n+      return { unavailableReason: \"fingerprint_failed\" };\n     }\n   }\n \n+  /** Backward-compatible fingerprint accessor; callers needing an explanation use the result form. */\n+  public getWorkspaceContextFingerprint(): string | undefined {\n+    return this.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult().fingerprint;\n+  }\n+\n   /** Judges, once per workspace, whether the session STARTED in a linked worktree the agent had already worked in. */\n   private judgeReceiptBaselineOnce(): void {\n     if (this.receiptBaselineJudged) return;\ndiff --git a/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts b/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\nindex e36f2e3a..21ecf59a 100644\n--- a/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\n+++ b/cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts\n@@ -289,6 +289,20 @@ const DEFAULT_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS = 2_000;\n const MAX_CONTEXT_BUDGET_MS = 30_000;\n const MAX_CONTEXT_ITEMS = 500;\n \n+class ContextSourceReadFailure extends Error {\n+  constructor(readonly safeDetail: string) { super(safeDetail); }\n+}\n+\n+function fingerprintUnavailableDetail(reason: string | undefined): string {\n+  switch (reason) {\n+    case \"program_settings_present\": return \"repository Git configuration contains program settings; fingerprinting was refused and freshness is unknown\";\n+    case \"configuration_unrecognized\": return \"repository Git configuration could not be safely interpreted; fingerprinting was refused and freshness is unknown\";\n+    case \"configuration_unavailable\": return \"repository Git configuration could not be inspected safely; fingerprinting was refused and freshness is unknown\";\n+    case \"fingerprint_failed\": return \"workspace fingerprint computation failed; freshness is unknown\";\n+    default: return \"workspace fingerprint API is unavailable; freshness is unknown\";\n+  }\n+}\n+\n async function context({ host, args, signal }: SlashContext): Promise<SlashOutcome> {\n   const [view, ...tokens] = args.trim().split(/\\s+/).filter(Boolean);\n   const usage = \"Usage: /context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>] | /context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]\";\n@@ -383,9 +397,10 @@ async function context({ host, args, signal }: SlashContext): Promise<SlashOutco\n         }\n         recordSourceItems(name, status, durationMs, result as SourceReadResult, detail);\n       }\n-    } catch {\n-      sources.push({ name, status: \"failed\", durationMs: performance.now() - started, items: [], detail: \"source lookup failed; no source content was recorded\" });\n-      gaps.push(`${name} source lookup failed`);\n+    } catch (error) {\n+      const detail = error instanceof ContextSourceReadFailure ? error.safeDetail : \"source lookup failed; no source content was recorded\";\n+      sources.push({ name, status: \"failed\", durationMs: performance.now() - started, items: [], detail });\n+      gaps.push(`${name} ${detail}`);\n     } finally {\n       if (timeout) clearTimeout(timeout);\n       if (abortListener) signal.removeEventListener(\"abort\", abortListener);\n@@ -411,9 +426,16 @@ async function context({ host, args, signal }: SlashContext): Promise<SlashOutco\n   });\n   let workspaceFingerprint: string | undefined;\n   await measure(\"workspace_state_fingerprint\", () => {\n-    if (typeof agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint !== \"function\") throw new Error(\"workspace fingerprint API unavailable\");\n-    workspaceFingerprint = agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint();\n-    if (!workspaceFingerprint) throw new Error(\"workspace fingerprint unavailable\");\n+    if (typeof agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult === \"function\") {\n+      const result = agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult();\n+      workspaceFingerprint = result.fingerprint;\n+      if (!workspaceFingerprint) throw new ContextSourceReadFailure(fingerprintUnavailableDetail(result.unavailableReason));\n+    } else if (typeof agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint === \"function\") {\n+      workspaceFingerprint = agent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprint();\n+      if (!workspaceFingerprint) throw new ContextSourceReadFailure(fingerprintUnavailableDetail(undefined));\n+    } else {\n+      throw new ContextSourceReadFailure(fingerprintUnavailableDetail(undefined));\n+    }\n     return [{\n       sourceType: \"workspace_state_fingerprint\",\n       sourceLocation: \"repository:candidate-identity\",\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c49-1bcf-7563-9889-443e19f9956a","create_time":1795503184.6081698}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":48752,"sampled_through_sequence":48748,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
