✖ Tool Error:\n4478:  ✖ a mutation after a passing verification invalidates it (2283.690697ms)\n4489:✖ Working: run_tests\n4490:✖ Tool Error:\n4520:✖ Working: write_file\n4521:✖ Tool Error:\n4546:  ✖ no applicable verifier: completion is honestly UNVERIFIED with an explicit reason (1797.015481ms)\n4548:✖ A-3 verifier-backed completion (17867.579119ms)\n4586:× TURN FAILED  execution=FAILED outcome=NOT_ESTABLISHED (INFERENCE_FAILED: stream_incomplete/transport; provider recovery exhausted after 2 submissions, 1s waiting — run `nexus doctor`, check LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT in ~/.config/nexus/config.env, or use /connect)\n4615:× TURN FAILED  execution=FAILED outcome=NOT_ESTABLISHED (INFERENCE_FAILED: provider_error_frame/provider; provider recovery exhausted after 2 submissions, 1s waiting — run `nexus doctor`, check LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT in ~/.config/nexus/config.env, or use /connect)\n4636:✖ Working: write_file\n4637:✖ Tool Error:\n4650:✖ Working: write_file\n4651:✖ Tool Error:\n4666:✖ Working: write_file\n4667:✖ Tool Error:\n4682:✖ Working: write_file\n4683:✖ Tool Error:\n4697:✖ Working: write_file\n4698:✖ Tool Error:\n4716:✖ Working: write_file\n4717:✖ Tool Error:\n4727:✖ Working: write_file\n4728:✖ Tool Error:\n4742:✖ Working: write_file\n4743:✖ Tool Error:\n4754:  ✖ delayed mutating loop: one cancel admits no new mutation and records INTERRUPTED (8105.818107ms)\n4756:✖ Inference provider temporarily unavailable\n4769:✖ Working: run_command\n4770:✖ Tool Error:\n4775:✖ Working: write_file\n4776:✖ Tool Error:\n4833:  ✖ cancel kills an in-flight command and prevents its queued tool call from dispatching (8085.771809ms)\n4838:✖ Inference request aborted by operator\n4850:✖ Inference request aborted by operator\n4873:✖ A-2 cancellation (19880.852825ms)\n4885:  ✖ TDD synthesizer verification uses the agent shell authority boundary (346.159627ms)\n4910:  ✖ RustCoreBridge executes run_tests tool with structured diagnostic output (49.245746ms)\n4926:  ✖ RustCoreBridge executes native git operations via git2 (Candidate #06) (133.745293ms)\n4927:  ✖ RustCoreBridge executes CST symbol parser and syntax navigation (Candidate #04) (95.026165ms)\n4928:  ✖ RustCoreBridge executes inverted trigram search acceleration (Candidate #10) (83.543018ms)\n4929:  ✖ RustCoreBridge executes commands via allocated Pseudo-Terminal (PTY) (Candidate #03) (88.342588ms)\n4930:  ✖ RustCoreBridge reads files via zero-copy memmap2 and counts lines (Candidate #07) (87.82044ms)\n4934:  ✖ RustCoreBridge executes outline_file tool for compact AST context conservation (94.465802ms)\n4948:✖ Nexus Code Test Suite (80533.924114ms)\n4953:  ✖ verified completion -> exit 0 (3169.607259ms)\n4954:  ✖ suite passing without testing the change -> exit 2 (3261.062332ms)\n4955:  ✖ completed without applicable verifier -> exit 2 (3034.450178ms)\n4959:  ✖ a global deliverable declaration before the command is retained by the run action (3455.618399ms)\n4960:✖ process exit contract (harness run) (23542.837487ms)\n4969:  ✖ Ctrl-C during a delayed mutating trajectory: one interrupt, no new mutation, prompt returns, next turn works (21685.904145ms)\n4973:✖ interactive REPL (pty) (29542.990663ms)\n5017:  ✖ an error the candidate introduced in a modified file blocks and names the configuration (2585.935535ms)\n5023:  ✖ an error that was already there in an untouched file is PREEXISTING, recorded, and does not block (1829.584024ms)\n5029:  ✖ a clean project passes, recorded under its tsconfig (1642.043048ms)\n5035:  ✖ no tsconfig: not applicable, outcome unchanged (1714.385127ms)\n5043:  ✖ an enforced solution-style tsconfig that this checker cannot run blocks completion (2267.579281ms)\n5053:  ✖ NEXUS_TYPECHECK=off disables the check (2056.409775ms)\n5061:  ✖ the HarnessConfig typecheck setting disables the check (2096.494898ms)\n5074:  ✖ an operator-configured verifier makes the check record-only unless NEXUS_TYPECHECK=enforce (2515.317475ms)\n5089:  ✖ tsc not installed is UNAVAILABLE and blocks an enforced check (PATH without tsc) (2773.268907ms)\n5097:  ✖ an unchanged failing type-check is not rerun: the skip names the typecheck command and keeps its evidence (2163.840741ms)\n5102:✖ type-check as verifier evidence: agent level (22469.638208ms)\n5118:  ✖ a burst of distinct writes stops at the objective tool budget and resume cannot raise it (1768.587927ms)\n5148:  ✖ a progressing task runs past 30 steps without the operator typing continue (5557.833542ms)\n5224:  ✖ a stuck task stops boundedly: recovery notes, then STAGNATION_DETECTED (2609.71625ms)\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:24:| Navigability | 2 — Exploratory | `/context inspect [--json]` reports source identity, scope, trust, freshness, retrieval reason/method, and coverage gaps. Bounded inference manifests reference the exact message positions and tool schemas handed to the adapter; current in-memory system-prompt sections link to `request:message:0`; session records and exports preserve the request references. | Message references identify position and role, not a stable semantic relationship graph. Prompt-section links are invalidated after prompt bytes change and are unavailable after resume until the prompt is rebuilt. The manifest proves the client-side handoff attempt, not provider receipt or processing. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:26:| Freshness | 1 — Ad hoc | Items carry explicit `current` / `stale` / `unknown` plus invalidation rules. Session and archive reconstruction marks history unknown. `/context inspect` records a bounded composite candidate fingerprint and compares it with the previous saved inventory; changed workspaces produce invalidated repository-item references and an explicit partial-coverage reason. Durable knowledge entries now explicitly report unknown freshness in inspection and prompt text because their opaque source references have no stored fingerprint or revalidation. | There is no per-source freshness identity for ignored environment inputs, tool policy, or individual memory provenance, and no measured change-to-invalidation objective. Memory freshness remains unknown; the system does not infer staleness or correctness from an opaque reference. |\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:40:- `ContextInventorySnapshot`: schema version, capture time, session/task/workspace identity, optional bounded composite workspace fingerprint and comparison outcome, item list, per-source timing/status/counts, estimate provenance, omissions, completeness, and reason for incomplete or unknown coverage. Timeout/cancellation is an additive `outcome` value while the existing `status` remains `failed`, so schema-1 readers continue to accept the inventory.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:43:- `/context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]` measures current client-visible sources on demand and optionally stores a content-free session snapshot; `/context maturity [--json]` accepts the same budget/item limits and emits a deterministic four-dimension assessment with evidence, gaps, limitations, and next improvements. The default total source-collection budget is 2,000 ms. The same budget applies sequentially across the whole collection pass, so source order is deterministic and remaining sources are marked timed out after exhaustion.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:64:6. Context inspection and maturity assessment are available through the shared REPL/TUI slash router and JSON output is parseable.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:72:- After the owner authorized takeover of stale claims, request capture was integrated at `AutonomousAgent.submitGuardingLength`; the same content-free manifest is saved through existing task/session persistence, exposed to `/context inspect`, and included in session exports. Recovered `dispatching` records become `unknown_effect`; no claim is made that this client-side record proves provider receipt.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:146:On exact source head `dafe4fa2` (base `db9f6f98`, `release/v1.3.0`), durable project knowledge context explicitly carries `freshness: unknown` and a reason in `/context inspect`; prompt rendering labels each retained entry `freshness: unknown` because its source references are not revalidated. Request manifest construction now derives the aggregate estimate from the same per-message and tool counts it records; a deterministic assertion matches `calculateContextBudget`, including tool calls and capped references. `npm run build` passed; `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 17/17; the provider wire matrix passed 90/90 on this head. `knowledge_memory_controls.test.ts` passed 3/3 and `slash_router.test.ts` 39/39 after the preceding memory-freshness change. A synthetic microbenchmark measured 50.4% lower local manifest-build time on its stated fixture; it is not an end-to-end throughput result. No source digest or memory invalidation mechanism was added.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:154:On the current candidate (`33e744c9`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `db9f6f98`), `tui_maturity_e2e.test.ts` passed 1/1 in 70.1 seconds, including the scripted multi-step turn, context inspection, resume, and export assertions. The same E2E test then passed 1/1 on the release baseline (`db9f6f98`) in 47.0 seconds. This was one sequential pair on the same host, not a randomized or repeated benchmark; the candidate took about 23 seconds longer in this sample. Treat this as a throughput regression signal requiring controlled repeated runs, not a causal attribution or a qualification failure. It supersedes the earlier statement above that the latest PTY run was still failed/unverified: functional TUI E2E now passes, while comparative performance and full-suite qualification remain open. Earlier timeout runs remain recorded as historical failures.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:217:Review of the context freshness path identified that `getWorkspaceContextFingerprint()` called `computeCandidateIdentitySync()` directly. Candidate identity uses Git commands, and repository or environment configuration can bind filters, fsmonitor, included configuration, or other program settings. Context inspection must not treat that risk as a documented limitation while still running those commands.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:219:`cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts` now uses bounded, non-following filesystem reads to inspect worktree metadata and repository, system, and global Git configuration before fingerprinting. It fails closed for command-bearing settings, included configuration, unsupported syntax, config-count overrides, and inaccessible config. `AutonomousAgent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult()` preserves a typed unavailability reason while the previous string-returning accessor remains compatible (`cli/src/agent.ts:1878-1892`). `/context inspect` records a failed source measurement and an explicit unknown-freshness reason instead of recording a current fingerprint (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:293-310,426-451`). This guard applies to the context fingerprint caller; it is not a general sandbox for other Git operations.\ndocs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md:221:The adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. On the current source changes, isolated `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 20/20 and `npm run build` passed. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. The source patch is on the implementation worktree and has not been rebased, committed, pushed, or independently reviewed; PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:301:    case \"fingerprint_failed\": return \"workspace fingerprint computation failed; freshness is unknown\";\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:302:    default: return \"workspace fingerprint API is unavailable; freshness is unknown\";\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:308:  const usage = \"Usage: /context inspect [--json] [--record] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>] | /context maturity [--json] [--budget-ms <1..30000>] [--max-items <1..500>]\";\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:333:  if (signal.aborted) return reply(\"context\", \"Context inspection was cancelled.\", false);\ncli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:577:    if (!savedSession) return reply(\"context\", \"No saved session exists to attach this inventory to. Run /save first, then /context inspect --record.\", false);\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":100787292}},"started_at_ms":1795505362219,"completed_at_ms":1795505363320}}
