{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:38:43.681Z","ordinal":109324,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","response_id":"resp_0f4fd85789ec756b016b053efeb02c87d2966313e7ed0a35ec","usage":{"input_tokens":73656,"cached_input_tokens":72192,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":140,"reasoning_output_tokens":38,"total_tokens":73796},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2365698,"cached_input_tokens":2323328,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5705,"reasoning_output_tokens":2224,"total_tokens":2371403},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2344862032,"cached_input_tokens":2326377088,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3860775,"reasoning_output_tokens":1859114,"total_tokens":2348722807}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:38:44.521Z","ordinal":109325,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-01c8e8a8-251c-41af-988b-1ffb8a6b769b","process_id":"66073","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '18,48p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; tail -n 10 \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log\""],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '18,48p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; tail -n 10 \"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n2026-11-24T04:25:00Z RELEASE P10_PLAN_EVIDENCE and FILE_docs_assurance_POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md: PR #768 merged as 55f1aac7; exact-head required checks passed and post-merge CI 45324705165 passed.\n2026-11-24T05:39:41Z CLAIM WP_P10_03_CANDIDATE_EXPORT_BINDING plus FILE_cli_src_audit_export.ts, FILE_cli_test_audit_export.test.ts, FILE_docs_assurance_POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md — codex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding — bounded current-candidate binding in audit exports.\n2026-11-24T06:15:49Z RELEASE SUITE-context-maturity-current-7b04317a — exact snapshot make test exited 0; Rust 53+406+9 passed, CLI 6,159 passed/0 failed/17 skipped, scope fixtures and security lifecycle gates passed; evaluator fixture roots absent.\n2026-11-24T06:19:55Z TAKEOVER CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM and CLAIM REDACTED.md — prior context-maturity owner PID 3065857 was absent; owner-authorized continuation on release/v1.3.0.\n2026-11-24T06:44:25Z\tCLAIM\tcodex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding\tFILE_cli_src_core_candidate.ts FILE_cli_test_candidate_git_paths.test.ts\n2026-11-24T06:44:26Z TAKEOVER FILE_cli_src_slash_workspace_commands.ts — stale PID 1288600 absent; owner-authorized continuation on codex/context-maturity-v130.\n2026-11-24T06:44:26Z TAKEOVER FILE_cli_test_context_inventory.test.ts — stale PID 1288600 absent; owner-authorized continuation on codex/context-maturity-v130.\n2026-11-24T06:44:26Z CLAIM FILE_cli_src_core_workspace_git_safety.ts — codex/context-maturity-v130 — fail-closed Git configuration preflight for context fingerprinting.\n2026-11-24T06:56:54Z CLAIM SUITE-context-maturity-19f34a0 — exact-head make test on isolated snapshot.\n2026-11-24T06:59:49Z NOTE SUITE-context-maturity-19f34a0 — initial make test attempt cancelled after Rust groups passed because clean snapshot had no cli/node_modules and required CI evaluator fixtures were unset; preparing pinned dependencies and make test-ci fixture preflight.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":612548798}},"started_at_ms":1795505923907,"completed_at_ms":1795505924520}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:38:44.656Z","ordinal":109326,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20c7e-2a2f-7140-89b6-1ea67898f718","call_id":"call_bf7dfa86001a48a88c60fefbe7e02ff2","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n2026-11-24T04:25:00Z RELEASE P10_PLAN_EVIDENCE and FILE_docs_assurance_POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md: PR #768 merged as 55f1aac7; exact-head required checks passed and post-merge CI 45324705165 passed.\n2026-11-24T05:39:41Z CLAIM WP_P10_03_CANDIDATE_EXPORT_BINDING plus FILE_cli_src_audit_export.ts, FILE_cli_test_audit_export.test.ts, FILE_docs_assurance_POWER_OF_TEN_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md — codex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding — bounded current-candidate binding in audit exports.\n2026-11-24T06:15:49Z RELEASE SUITE-context-maturity-current-7b04317a — exact snapshot make test exited 0; Rust 53+406+9 passed, CLI 6,159 passed/0 failed/17 skipped, scope fixtures and security lifecycle gates passed; evaluator fixture roots absent.\n2026-11-24T06:19:55Z TAKEOVER CTX_MATURITY_SYSTEM and CLAIM REDACTED.md — prior context-maturity owner PID 3065857 was absent; owner-authorized continuation on release/v1.3.0.\n2026-11-24T06:44:25Z\tCLAIM\tcodex/p10-03-audit-candidate-binding\tFILE_cli_src_core_candidate.ts FILE_cli_test_candidate_git_paths.test.ts\n2026-11-24T06:44:26Z TAKEOVER FILE_cli_src_slash_workspace_commands.ts — stale PID 1288600 absent; owner-authorized continuation on codex/context-maturity-v130.\n2026-11-24T06:44:26Z TAKEOVER FILE_cli_test_context_inventory.test.ts — stale PID 1288600 absent; owner-authorized continuation on codex/context-maturity-v130.\n2026-11-24T06:44:26Z CLAIM FILE_cli_src_core_workspace_git_safety.ts — codex/context-maturity-v130 — fail-closed Git configuration preflight for context fingerprinting.\n2026-11-24T06:56:54Z CLAIM SUITE-context-maturity-19f34a0 — exact-head make test on isolated snapshot.\n2026-11-24T06:59:49Z NOTE SUITE-context-maturity-19f34a0 — initial make test attempt cancelled after Rust groups passed because clean snapshot had no cli/node_modules and required CI evaluator fixtures were unset; preparing pinned dependencies and make test-ci fixture preflight.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","create_time":1795505924.6559052}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":49174,"sampled_through_sequence":49171,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
