{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:39:53.660Z","ordinal":109378,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b053f3d9c4c87d2bda990d862187b13","status":"completed","call_id":"call_b8258520b94d4df7a6f5ae7b0951595c","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md\\n@@\\n-The adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. On the current source changes, isolated `context_inventory.test.ts` passed 20/20 and `npm run build` passed. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. The source patch is on the implementation worktree and has not been rebased, committed, pushed, or independently reviewed; PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\\n+The adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\\n+\\n+### Rebased security fix qualification — `release/v1.3.0`\\n+\\n+The security fix is committed locally as `19f34a0210b52fed0d86bc2cf474c93e6deeb37a` on `codex/context-maturity-v130`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `5abbc4cbb24a2601b8b1c70acc908a90f73926df`. On this exact source head, `node --import tsx --test test/context_inventory.test.ts` passed 20/20 and `npm run build` passed. `make build` had also passed on a detached snapshot of this same head.\\n+\\n+An isolated-snapshot `make test` was started at this head but interrupted by its owner after more than 23 minutes because repeated provider-recovery cases could not persist checkpoints and Rust-core RPC daemon disconnects made multiple CLI integration tests fail. The partial run also reported other test assertion failures; because it was interrupted, there is no complete test count or terminal suite result. Its local partial log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-19f34a02-built.log`. This is not a passing full-suite result, and this branch is not fully qualified. Evaluator fixture-backed checks could not be qualified because the required mount/runtime fixture was unavailable and was not replaced. The prior complete passing suite applies only to `7b04317a` on its older release base. Hosted checks, independent review, installed acceptance, and comparative held-out evaluation remain outstanding. The code and docs are not pushed; no PR, merge, or tag was performed.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","create_time":1795505981.6282403}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":49198,"sampled_through_sequence":49196,"client_authored":false}}
