{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:46:12.259Z","ordinal":109575,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0540b559c487d292383d5c013091ac","status":"completed","call_id":"call_87bb072e90634e15843a93a9003f7287","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130/docs/v1.3.0/PLAN.md\\n@@\\n-CE-1 is a new context-quality trail. Its inventory, guarded memory controls, request manifests, bounded collection budget, and repository-fingerprint comparison are implemented on the `release/v1.3.0` work branch. An earlier full `make test` passed on detached snapshot `eda532061b8f78c67ddc3ffe4e3c3621312fd4eb`, but predates later context changes. On snapshot `361a744f` (release base `56e644cf`), the follow-up full suite exited 2: core Rust 53/53, TUI 406/406, scope fixtures, and security gates passed; both CLI shards timed out, with 10 other reported failures. The context continuity file passed directly 34/34 in 532.959 seconds, longer than the test runner's 300-second file limit. Several evaluator failures refused qualification because compiler exposure could not be checked; all failures and the second shard timeout remain unclassified. The release branch later advanced to `51bf3db7`; source-tested head `8d4bb77a` is rebased there. On this source head, `make build`, context inventory 17/17, memory controls 3/3, provider wire matrix 90/90, audit export 18/18, and session durability 4/4 passed. The subsequent commit only updates qualification documentation; the full suite has not run on the latest source head. See [`CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md`](../research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md) for exact evidence and limitations. Remaining qualification includes full suite on the latest source head, resolution of suite timeout and evaluator failures, independent review, hosted and installed acceptance, source-specific non-repository freshness, measured retrieval percentiles/SLO, and held-out durable-memory value. Memory freshness remains explicitly unknown where its references cannot be revalidated. CE-1 reuses the existing client and session architecture and does not depend on changing inference providers.\\n+CE-1 is implemented in the local `codex/context-maturity-v130` work branch, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `5abbc4cbb24a2601b8b1c70acc908a90f73926df`. Security follow-up `19f34a0210b52fed0d86bc2cf474c93e6deeb37a` makes context fingerprinting refuse command-bearing or uninspectable Git configuration; no provider code changed. Exact-head evidence: `make build` passed on a detached snapshot; `context_inventory.test.ts` 20/20, `provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` 90/90, and `workflow_provider_neutral.test.ts` 3/3 passed; CLI `npm run build` passed. A full `make test` on the exact source head was interrupted by its owner after more than 23 minutes following multiple failures, repeated provider-recovery checkpoint persistence errors, and Rust-core RPC daemon disconnects; it has no complete result and does not qualify this branch. Required evaluator mount/runtime fixtures were unavailable and were not substituted. Earlier green suites apply only to older commits. See [`CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md`](../research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md) for detailed evidence and logs. Remaining qualification includes diagnosing the full-suite failures and running it to completion, the required evaluator fixtures, independent review, hosted checks, installed acceptance, source-specific non-repository freshness, measured retrieval percentiles/SLO, and held-out evidence of durable-memory value. Memory freshness remains explicitly unknown where references cannot be revalidated. CE-1 uses the existing client/session architecture and does not depend on changing inference providers.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","create_time":1795506357.3522744}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":49286,"sampled_through_sequence":49284,"client_authored":false}}
