{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:50:59.960Z","ordinal":109688,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0541e1cab487d281238feeb76d2a5a","status":"completed","call_id":"call_07fbbb2b7b3f40099d474c728eeac7cc","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"nl -ba cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts | sed -n '1,12p'; nl -ba docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | tail -n 12; ps -p 2874970,2875457,2881709,2881726 -o pid,stat,args\",\"workdir\":\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1200}); text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","create_time":1795506657.7942352}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":49338,"sampled_through_sequence":49336,"client_authored":false}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:51:00.016Z","ordinal":109689,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","session_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","root_turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","response_id":"resp_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0541d653ec87d28e3a4875a03ff896","usage":{"input_tokens":108974,"cached_input_tokens":108416,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":611,"reasoning_output_tokens":481,"total_tokens":109585},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":7207432,"cached_input_tokens":7120512,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":21853,"reasoning_output_tokens":10028,"total_tokens":7229285},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2349703766,"cached_input_tokens":2331174272,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3876923,"reasoning_output_tokens":1866918,"total_tokens":2353580689}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:51:01.031Z","ordinal":109690,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dea2c003-aaa2-4031-ad2c-1314b55ea2f5","process_id":"23175","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","nl -ba cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts | sed -n '1,12p'; nl -ba docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | tail -n 12; ps -p 2874970,2875457,2881709,2881726 -o pid,stat,args"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/context-maturity-v130","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"nl -ba cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts | sed -n '1,12p'; nl -ba docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-MATURITY-SYSTEM.md | tail -n 12; ps -p 2874970,2875457,2881709,2881726 -o pid,stat,args"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"     1\timport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\n     2\timport * as path from \"node:path\";\n     3\timport { parseGitfilePointer, readSmallFile, verifyCheckout } from \"./checkout_trust.js\";\n     4\t\n     5\tconst MAX_GIT_CONFIG_BYTES = 1024 * 1024;\n     6\t\n     7\texport type WorkspaceGitSafetyReason = \"program_settings_present\" | \"configuration_unavailable\" | \"configuration_unrecognized\" | \"fingerprint_failed\";\n     8\texport type WorkspaceGitSafety =\n     9\t  | { safe: true }\n    10\t  | { safe: false; reason: Exclude<WorkspaceGitSafetyReason, \"fingerprint_failed\"> };\n    11\t\n    12\tfunction findGitDir(workspace: string): string | undefined {\n   216\t\n   217\tReview of the context freshness path identified that `getWorkspaceContextFingerprint()` called `computeCandidateIdentitySync()` directly. Candidate identity uses Git commands, and repository or environment configuration can bind filters, fsmonitor, included configuration, or other program settings. Context inspection must not treat that risk as a documented limitation while still running those commands.\n   218\t\n   219\t`cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts` now uses bounded, non-following filesystem reads to inspect worktree metadata and repository, system, and global Git configuration before fingerprinting. It fails closed for command-bearing settings, included configuration, unsupported syntax, config-count overrides, and inaccessible config. `AutonomousAgent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult()` preserves a typed unavailability reason while the previous string-returning accessor remains compatible (`cli/src/agent.ts:1878-1892`). `/context inspect` records a failed source measurement and an explicit unknown-freshness reason instead of recording a current fingerprint (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:293-310,426-451`). This guard applies to the context fingerprint caller; it is not a general sandbox for other Git operations.\n   220\t\n   221\tThe adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\n   222\t\n   223\t### Rebased security fix qualification — `release/v1.3.0`\n   224\t\n   225\tThe security fix is committed locally as `19f34a0210b52fed0d86bc2cf474c93e6deeb37a` on `codex/context-maturity-v130`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `5abbc4cbb24a2601b8b1c70acc908a90f73926df`. On this exact source head, `node --import tsx --test test/context_inventory.test.ts` passed 20/20, `node --import tsx --test test/provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` passed 90/90, `node --import tsx --test test/workflow_provider_neutral.test.ts` passed 3/3, `node --import tsx --test test/harness.test.ts` passed 90/90 in serial isolation, and `npm run build` passed. `make build` had also passed on a detached snapshot of this same head. The isolated harness result did not reproduce the Rust-core RPC daemon disconnects observed during the interrupted multi-file run; their cause remains unclassified. These provider fixtures exercise multiple adapter request/reply contracts and a minimal local OpenAI-compatible workflow; they do not qualify live provider services or replace the full system workflow evaluation.\n   226\t\n   227\tAn isolated-snapshot `make test` was started at this head but interrupted by its owner after more than 23 minutes because repeated provider-recovery cases could not persist checkpoints and Rust-core RPC daemon disconnects made multiple CLI integration tests fail. The partial run also reported other test assertion failures; because it was interrupted, there is no complete test count or terminal suite result. Its local partial log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-19f34a02-built.log`. This is not a passing full-suite result, and this branch is not fully qualified. Evaluator fixture-backed checks could not be qualified because the required mount/runtime fixture was unavailable and was not replaced. The prior complete passing suite applies only to `7b04317a` on its older release base. Hosted checks, independent review, installed acceptance, and comparative held-out evaluation remain outstanding. The code and docs are not pushed; no PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n    PID STAT COMMAND\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":809451518}},"started_at_ms":1795506660221,"completed_at_ms":1795506661031}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:51:01.169Z","ordinal":109691,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a20c89-6731-77c0-acdb-e672b4d99cfc","call_id":"call_07fbbb2b7b3f40099d474c728eeac7cc","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"     1\timport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\n     2\timport * as path from \"node:path\";\n     3\timport { parseGitfilePointer, readSmallFile, verifyCheckout } from \"./checkout_trust.js\";\n     4\t\n     5\tconst MAX_GIT_CONFIG_BYTES = 1024 * 1024;\n     6\t\n     7\texport type WorkspaceGitSafetyReason = \"program_settings_present\" | \"configuration_unavailable\" | \"configuration_unrecognized\" | \"fingerprint_failed\";\n     8\texport type WorkspaceGitSafety =\n     9\t  | { safe: true }\n    10\t  | { safe: false; reason: Exclude<WorkspaceGitSafetyReason, \"fingerprint_failed\"> };\n    11\t\n    12\tfunction findGitDir(workspace: string): string | undefined {\n   216\t\n   217\tReview of the context freshness path identified that `getWorkspaceContextFingerprint()` called `computeCandidateIdentitySync()` directly. Candidate identity uses Git commands, and repository or environment configuration can bind filters, fsmonitor, included configuration, or other program settings. Context inspection must not treat that risk as a documented limitation while still running those commands.\n   218\t\n   219\t`cli/src/core/workspace_git_safety.ts` now uses bounded, non-following filesystem reads to inspect worktree metadata and repository, system, and global Git configuration before fingerprinting. It fails closed for command-bearing settings, included configuration, unsupported syntax, config-count overrides, and inaccessible config. `AutonomousAgent.getWorkspaceContextFingerprintResult()` preserves a typed unavailability reason while the previous string-returning accessor remains compatible (`cli/src/agent.ts:1878-1892`). `/context inspect` records a failed source measurement and an explicit unknown-freshness reason instead of recording a current fingerprint (`cli/src/slash/workspace_commands.ts:293-310,426-451`). This guard applies to the context fingerprint caller; it is not a general sandbox for other Git operations.\n   220\t\n   221\tThe adversarial fixtures plant a clean filter, fsmonitor command, included config, and global clean filter, and assert that marker commands do not run. An end-to-end `/context inspect` fixture verifies unavailable fingerprint status and the surfaced reason. A prior test's success fixture depended on fingerprinting the full development checkout and its incidental generated files; it now uses a minimal temporary Git repository. No provider adapter or inference provider was changed. Maturity ratings remain unchanged. PRs #771/#772 remain open and are owned by the review/merge agent.\n   222\t\n   223\t### Rebased security fix qualification — `release/v1.3.0`\n   224\t\n   225\tThe security fix is committed locally as `19f34a0210b52fed0d86bc2cf474c93e6deeb37a` on `codex/context-maturity-v130`, based on `release/v1.3.0` at `5abbc4cbb24a2601b8b1c70acc908a90f73926df`. On this exact source head, `node --import tsx --test test/context_inventory.test.ts` passed 20/20, `node --import tsx --test test/provider_wire_matrix.test.ts` passed 90/90, `node --import tsx --test test/workflow_provider_neutral.test.ts` passed 3/3, `node --import tsx --test test/harness.test.ts` passed 90/90 in serial isolation, and `npm run build` passed. `make build` had also passed on a detached snapshot of this same head. The isolated harness result did not reproduce the Rust-core RPC daemon disconnects observed during the interrupted multi-file run; their cause remains unclassified. These provider fixtures exercise multiple adapter request/reply contracts and a minimal local OpenAI-compatible workflow; they do not qualify live provider services or replace the full system workflow evaluation.\n   226\t\n   227\tAn isolated-snapshot `make test` was started at this head but interrupted by its owner after more than 23 minutes because repeated provider-recovery cases could not persist checkpoints and Rust-core RPC daemon disconnects made multiple CLI integration tests fail. The partial run also reported other test assertion failures; because it was interrupted, there is no complete test count or terminal suite result. Its local partial log is `/tmp/context-maturity-make-test-19f34a02-built.log`. This is not a passing full-suite result, and this branch is not fully qualified. Evaluator fixture-backed checks could not be qualified because the required mount/runtime fixture was unavailable and was not replaced. The prior complete passing suite applies only to `7b04317a` on its older release base. Hosted checks, independent review, installed acceptance, and comparative held-out evaluation remain outstanding. The code and docs are not pushed; no PR, merge, or tag was performed.\n    PID STAT COMMAND\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","create_time":1795506661.1695955}},"metadata":{"history_sequence":49339,"sampled_through_sequence":49336,"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:51:01.172Z","ordinal":109692,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"token_count","info":{"total_token_usage":{"input_tokens":2335016120,"cached_input_tokens":2316559872,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3718227,"reasoning_output_tokens":1866918,"total_tokens":2338734347},"last_token_usage":{"input_tokens":108974,"cached_input_tokens":108416,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":611,"reasoning_output_tokens":481,"total_tokens":109585},"last_usage_includes_reasoning":true,"model_context_window":258400},"rate_limits":{"limit_id":"codex","limit_name":null,"primary":{"used_percent":4.0,"window_minutes":300,"resets_at":1795523281},"secondary":{"used_percent":90.0,"window_minutes":10080,"resets_at":1795899429},"credits":{"has_credits":false,"unlimited":false,"balance":"0"},"individual_limit":null,"spend_control_reached":null,"plan_type":"plus","rate_limit_reached_type":null}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-11-24T07:51:08.685Z","ordinal":109693,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1f54f-2cb2-7201-ad27-acf2d9bbd90e","turn_id":"01a20c6e-33b2-7660-a7f0-668b82778aee","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0f4fd85789ec756b016b0541e8004087d2a0d962a9f9bd93ef","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I continued the context maturity work on `codex/context-maturity-v130`, based on `release/v1.3.0`.\n\nThe main change is a fail-closed Git configuration check before context freshness fingerprinting. It prevents fingerprinting from running when Git settings could execute commands, and reports freshness as unknown when configuration cannot be safely inspected. The fix and its adversarial tests are committed as `19f34a02`. I also updated the roadmap and qualification notes in later local commits.\n\nOn that source head, the context tests passed **20/20**, the provider wire matrix **90/90**, provider-neutral workflow **3/3**, and the isolated harness suite **90/90**; the CLI build passed. The full `make test` run was interrupted after more than 23 minutes with multiple failures and repeated provider-recovery and RPC errors. It has no complete result, so the branch is **not fully qualified**. The evaluator fixtures, independent review, hosted checks, installed acceptance, and comparative evaluation remain outstanding.\n\nI have not pushed or opened a PR. The owner checkout remains untouched; the implementation worktree has two untracked generated directories, `.cargo-target-context-maturity/` and `cli/.local/`, which I left in place."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"content_token_count":256,"started_at_ms":1795506664022,"completed_at_ms":1795506668685}}
